#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""build-slot: machine-wide admission for heavy jobs (builds, full test suites, sweeps).

Every agent and person on a shared machine runs heavy work through this gate, so the
machine is never driven to load 100 with no free memory, where every build crawls:

    build-slot -- python3 x.py build --stage 1 compiler/rustc library
    build-slot -- targo --unverified test -p ay-dpll
    build-slot --cpus 24 -- python3 x.py build --stage 1 compiler/rustc
    build-slot --wait-timeout 180 -- targo --unverified test -p ay-dpll
    build-slot --exclusive --wait-timeout 1800 -- <quiet-window command>
    build-slot adopt <existing-direct-job-pid>
    build-slot --rank release --claim-key trust-train:mint --wide -- <command>
    build-slot status

One admission authority on aterm hosts (not yet in effect on any host):
  * When this host's aterm answers `aterm pkg claim --capabilities` with
    aterm-claim-exec-v1 (found as BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI, else `aterm` on PATH),
    a fresh admission is exactly one claim in aterm's capacity ledger, held for
    the command's whole process tree. No slot, FIFO ticket, epoch fence or
    borrowed share is taken, so nothing is held while that claim waits, and the
    targo builds it covers claim nothing again. The command gets the ledger's
    core grant as CARGO_BUILD_JOBS, TARGO_PLANNED_JOBS and TARGO_CALLER_JOBS.
    No released aterm has that verb yet (2026-11-17), so every host still
    admits through the slot pool below; docs/BUILD_SLOT.md has the contract.
  * --rank ordinary|release (default ordinary) and --claim-key K name the
    claim's rank and the key whose measured peak sizes its memory claim
    (default: one key per program and checkout). --cpus N asks for N cores;
    --wide asks for the host's; otherwise the claim asks for one pool share.
    --mem-gb (or BUILD_SLOT_MEM_GB) is the memory claimed; without either the
    ledger sizes it from the key's measured peak. --exclusive is one ALONE
    claim under which build-slot's own quiet-machine wait runs before the
    command. --wait-timeout bounds the whole ledger wait. The verb takes the
    per-worktree lock together with its admission, so a waiting claim holds
    neither capacity nor the worktree.
  * Where aterm is absent or answers that it has no such verb (exit 2), the
    slot pool below admits, after one stderr line saying why. Any other answer
    (a timeout, another exit, another reply) refuses: the authority is unknown,
    and nothing is started. `adopt` refuses where the ledger admits.
    `status` names the authority. `build-slot --capabilities` answers
    build-slot-claim-v1: this copy takes --rank, --claim-key and --wide.

The slot pool, where the ledger is unavailable:
  * At most --slots heavy jobs run at once, machine-wide. The default is one per 6
    CPUs, overridable with BUILD_SLOTS.
  * A job starts only while at least --mem-gb GiB is available (free + inactive +
    purgeable + speculative pages). The default is 8 GiB, overridable with
    BUILD_SLOT_MEM_GB.
  * --exclusive reserves every slot in the canonical host pool, including when
    --slots or BUILD_SLOTS is smaller. Its default CPU budget spans the host; it does not
    waive the command's own quiet/load/memory guards or stop unmanaged work.
    Workers must share BUILD_SLOT_DIR and the configured pool; an independently
    enlarged peer pool may use higher-numbered slots outside this reservation.
  * Exclusive admission also covers historic slot files and requires measured
    memory, load1 <= 0.35 * CPUs and no compiler/build processes for 10 seconds.
    Nested commands retain an already-exclusive reservation without establishing
    fresh quietness.
  * --wait-timeout bounds a fresh ordinary, native or exclusive admission. Timeout
    releases this unlaunched request; it never cancels another job or a running child.
    Nested, adopted and coordinated shared-memory requests cannot select this option.
  * --execution-start-fd takes one original nonblocking pipe writer for lifecycle
    observation, not admission. After the real child is created it reports `S`,
    its eight-byte big-endian PID, and the pre-spawn CLOCK_MONOTONIC microseconds
    as eight big-endian bytes, then closes. The payload never receives the pipe.
    Adoption and coordinated shared-memory wrappers cannot select this option.
  * Inside a git worktree, only one build-slot job runs at a time per worktree, so two
    agents that land in the same worktree queue instead of killing each other's builds.
  * Shared commands using Clean's structured `heavy_gate.sh run GB LABEL -- ...`
    wrapper wait for memory before claiming CPU. CPU contention rolls memory back
    immediately; old CPU-first callers therefore cannot form a mixed-order deadlock.
  * --cpus N atomically reserves the matching shared slots and grants N CPUs.
    Smaller explicit caller caps are retained; adopted jobs cannot be resized.
    An exclusive command defaults to the whole host CPU budget. --wide is the
    uncapped default here: borrowing below.
  * The child gets CARGO_BUILD_JOBS bounded by its share of the CPUs. A smaller
    positive caller request is preserved; a larger one is capped, and malformed
    requests refuse before admission.
  * With no caller CPU cap, admission borrows the currently free slots. Each
    borrowed share needs measured memory headroom; unknown memory keeps one
    share. Queued peers that fit beside the actual minimum retain room before
    optional borrowing. Borrowed shares remain leased through command exit, including if
    the gate dies. This is admission-time sizing, not runtime lease revocation.
  * Inside an aterm session, an admitted command runs through aterm's
    authenticated resource runner when the host advertises one, so its resource
    use is attributed to that session; otherwise it runs unchanged and unreported.
  * Among queued jobs, the oldest currently eligible request gets admission. A busy
    worktree or insufficient memory does not idle slots another request can use.
    An eligible multi-slot request reserves drain against later arrivals until
    its whole CPU claim fits, without exclusive admission's quiet-machine guards.
    An eligible exclusive request waits for the pool to drain before newer jobs run.
    `status` shows pending requests and their exclusive/resource requirements, so free
    slots held for that reservation are distinguishable from an idle queue. It observes
    ticket leases without changing admission order or retiring tickets.
  * The locks use the Unix account home independently of a private HOME/TMPDIR.
    BUILD_SLOT_DIR explicitly overrides this canonical pool and is inherited by children.
    The actual
    command inherits the leases, so a dead gate supervisor cannot free a slot while
    its command still runs. The kernel releases a lease after its last holder exits.
  * Every namespace directory it makes, ancestors included, is 0700 whatever the
    umask. An existing namespace directory writable by its group or others is
    refused with the `chmod go-w` that repairs it; build-slot never changes it.
  * Nested use is free: a child of a build-slot job (BUILD_SLOT_HELD=1) runs at once.
    A nested --exclusive requires an already exclusive parent; it cannot upgrade
    a shared admission. Use --exclusive on the outermost invocation.
  * `adopt PID` accounts for an existing unleased job without a watcher or a new
    command. Run it from that direct job's exact working directory, using the
    same canonical pool. Native PID/UID/birth/executable and cwd queries must
    succeed, and the job must belong to this user. Adopted leases remain held
    after this command exits, until that process exits or its PID is reused.
    Uncertain identity remains held; an exec by the same process does not free
    it. Repeating adoption repairs an interrupted publication without taking
    another slot. Adoption grants no CPU share, proof claim, or process control.

The exit status is the command's own; 128+N if it was killed by signal N.
"""
import errno
import fcntl
import hashlib
import importlib.util
import json
import math
import os
import pwd

import re
import select
import shutil
import signal
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import secrets
import shlex
from urllib.parse import unquote_to_bytes
from contextlib import contextmanager

DIR = None
MEASURED_NCPU = os.cpu_count()
NCPU = MEASURED_NCPU or 4
QUIET_LOAD_FRACTION = 0.35
QUIET_SECONDS = 10.0
# What this copy answers to `--capabilities`: it takes --rank, --claim-key and --wide.
CLAIM_WORDS_PROTOCOL = "build-slot-claim-v1"
# What an aterm whose capacity ledger can hold build-slot's one claim answers.
LEDGER_CLAIM_PROTOCOL = "aterm-claim-exec-v1"
RANKS = ("ordinary", "release")
CLAIM_KEY = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:/@+-]{0,199}")
# The bound on `aterm pkg claim --capabilities`. Under a load of 96 on 36 cores a
# process start can take seconds; past this the authority is unknown and refuses.
LEDGER_PROBE_SECONDS = 30.0
# How long past its --wait-ms the verb has to answer before build-slot stops it.
LEDGER_ANSWER_GRACE = 30.0
# How long a stopped verb's group has to exit after TERM before KILL.
LEDGER_STOP_GRACE = 10.0
# Clean's heavy_gate retries a coordinated attempt that found no room: first after
# 0.1 s, doubling to this, so a busy machine is not asked ten times a second.
MEMORY_RETRY_MAX = 2.0


class AdmissionTimeout(Exception):
    pass


class LedgerUnavailable(Exception):
    """No aterm here, or one without the verb: the slot pool admits (one stderr line)."""


class LedgerRefused(Exception):
    """aterm answered the probe otherwise: which authority admits is unknown, so nothing starts."""


class AdmissionUnavailable(Exception):
    """A coordinated memory holder must roll back instead of waiting for CPU."""
    pass


# Tests replace only this entrypoint, retaining their private account/pool probes.
_REEXEC = None
_EXIT_OWNER = None
RESOURCE_FD_HANDOFF_VERSION = 1


def resource_transport_owner():
    """Share the maintained descriptor parser and original-child observer."""
    global _EXIT_OWNER
    if _EXIT_OWNER is None:
        path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)),
                            "lib", "landing_targo.py")
        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("build_slot_exit_owner", path)
        owner = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
        # This source-controlled helper owns transport and child observation.
        # Execute its captured bytes, never an ignored timestamp-matching .pyc.
        with open(path, "rb") as source:
            code = source.read()
        exec(compile(code, path, "exec", dont_inherit=True), owner.__dict__)
        _EXIT_OWNER = owner
    return _EXIT_OWNER


def inherited_resource_fds(env):
    """Forward only declared live transport; its native owner judges authority."""
    try:
        return resource_transport_owner().resource_fds(env)
    except (OSError, ImportError, AttributeError, RuntimeError) as error:
        raise NamespaceError(f"inherited resource transport refused: {error}") from error


def original_child_exit_observer():
    """Require exclusive reaping and reuse the maintained native exit observer.

    The unreaped original child pins its group identity until forwarding is
    disabled. Neither Popen.returncode nor a later PID lookup supplies that.
    """
    try:
        if signal.getsignal(signal.SIGCHLD) != signal.SIG_DFL:
            raise RuntimeError("SIGCHLD must retain the original child for its sole reaper")
        owner = resource_transport_owner()
        if not owner.exit_observation_available():
            raise RuntimeError("native nonreaping child observation is unavailable")
        return owner.wait_child_exit
    except (OSError, ImportError, AttributeError, RuntimeError) as error:
        print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — cannot retain original child group: {error}",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return None


def memory_wrapper(cmd):
    """Recognize Clean's structured shared wrapper without parsing shell text."""
    offset = 1 if cmd and os.path.basename(cmd[0]) in ("bash", "sh") else 0
    if (len(cmd) < offset + 5
            or os.path.basename(cmd[offset]) != "heavy_gate.sh"
            or cmd[offset + 1] != "run"):
        return None
    split = offset + 4
    if cmd[split] == "--":
        split += 1
    if split >= len(cmd):
        return None
    return cmd[:offset + 4], cmd[split:]


def coordinate_memory(options, wrapper):
    """Wait for memory with no CPU lease; roll it back if CPU cannot start.

    Old CPU-first callers remain safe: a new memory holder never waits for
    their CPU slots. Failed retries use the existing nonzero peak-history rule.
    The pipe distinguishes admission failure from a payload's real exit 75.
    """
    prefix, payload = wrapper
    observe_exit = original_child_exit_observer()
    if observe_exit is None:
        return 2
    reexec = _REEXEC or [sys.executable, "-I", "-B", os.path.abspath(__file__)]
    interrupted = None
    child = None
    # The pool orders attempts by this registry arrival; aterm's ledger by the
    # wall-clock arrival, so a retried look keeps its place among the claims.
    since_ms = time.time_ns() // 1_000_000
    delay = 0.1
    with admission_registry() as directory:
        live = [int(name[5:]) for name in os.listdir(directory)
                if name.startswith("wait-") and name[5:].isdigit()]
        arrival = next_admission_order(directory, live)

    def forward(sig, _frame):
        nonlocal interrupted
        interrupted = sig
        if child is not None:
            resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, sig)

    previous = {sig: signal.signal(sig, forward)
                for sig in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP)}
    try:
        while interrupted is None:
            reader, writer = os.pipe()
            os.set_blocking(reader, False)
            try:
                if interrupted is not None:
                    return 128 + interrupted
                command = [*prefix, "--", *reexec, "--_memory-attempt", str(writer), str(arrival),
                           "--_memory-since-ms", str(since_ms), *options, "--", *payload]
                child = subprocess.Popen(
                    command, start_new_session=True,
                    pass_fds=sorted({writer, *inherited_resource_fds(os.environ)}))
                if interrupted is not None:
                    forward(interrupted, None)
                os.close(writer)
                writer = None
                original = child
                observe_exit(original.pid)
                # Stop forwarding BEFORE the only owning wait can recycle the
                # group identity, including inside Popen's returncode update.
                child = None
                rc = original.wait()
                try:
                    marker = os.read(reader, 3)
                except BlockingIOError:
                    marker = b""
            finally:
                if writer is not None:
                    os.close(writer)
                os.close(reader)
                child = None
            if interrupted is not None:
                return 128 + interrupted
            if marker not in (b"", b"W", b"WR"):
                print("build-slot: invalid coordinated admission reply", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            if rc != 75 or marker != b"W":
                return 128 - rc if rc < 0 else rc
            # heavy_gate has already released memory before this retry. Each
            # attempt starts heavy_gate, build-slot and (on a ledger host) two
            # aterm processes, so a long wait backs off to MEMORY_RETRY_MAX.
            time.sleep(delay)
            delay = min(MEMORY_RETRY_MAX, delay * 2)
        return 128 + interrupted
    finally:
        for sig, handler in previous.items():
            signal.signal(sig, handler)



class NamespaceError(ValueError):
    pass


class CpuBridgeUnavailable(ValueError):
    pass


def worker_invocation(cmd):
    """Split only a direct Targo or its exact native, unplaced shim front."""
    if not cmd:
        return None
    front = (os.path.basename(cmd[0]) == "atpkg"
             and (list(cmd[1:2]) == ["__build_admit"]
                  or list(cmd[1:3]) == ["--private-state-root", "__build_admit"]))
    if front:
        if (len(cmd) < 6
                or list(cmd[1:5]) != ["__build_admit", "--shim", "targo", "-"]
                or not os.path.isabs(cmd[5])
                or os.path.basename(cmd[5]) != "targo"):
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("unsupported native Targo shim-front shape; no command was started")
        prefix, args = list(cmd[:6]), list(cmd[6:])
    elif os.path.basename(cmd[0]) == "targo":
        prefix, args = list(cmd[:1]), list(cmd[1:])
    else:
        return None
    if args[:1] == ["--resource-worker-v2"]:
        args = args[1:]
    # Targo's native parser owns the whole invocation, including globals,
    # aliases and harness data. A second spelling parser here silently routed
    # valid global-config compile commands into fixed admission. Query the
    # original words; only its strict reply decides support or refusal.
    return prefix, args


def worker_command(cmd):
    """Install one mandatory worker flag after the same supported native front."""
    invocation = worker_invocation(cmd)
    if invocation is None:
        return None
    prefix, args = invocation
    return [*prefix, "--resource-worker-v2", *args]


def bounded_native_query(query, *, timeout=2, limit=8192, observation=None,
                         purpose="capability discovery"):
    """Bound both streams and retain the original child group through its reap."""
    program = query[0]
    # An invalid transport is a refusal, never a reason to downgrade to fixed
    # admission after the selected frontend's capability could not be queried.
    passed = inherited_resource_fds(os.environ)
    observe_exit = original_child_exit_observer()
    if observe_exit is None:
        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("native discovery cannot retain its original child group")
    child = None
    reaped = False
    output = bytearray()
    diagnostic = bytearray()

    def refused(reason):
        detail = diagnostic.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
        reply = output.decode("utf-8", errors="replace")
        return CpuBridgeUnavailable(
            f"selected Targo {program!r} {purpose} {reason}; "
            f"stdout={reply!r}; stderr={detail!r}; no command was started")

    try:
        end = time.monotonic() + timeout
        child = subprocess.Popen(query, start_new_session=True,
                                 stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                                 stderr=subprocess.PIPE, pass_fds=passed)
        os.set_blocking(child.stdout.fileno(), False)
        os.set_blocking(child.stderr.fileno(), False)
        eof = set()
        while time.monotonic() < end:
            # Drain both bounded channels, including a diagnostic-only failure,
            # so a full stderr pipe cannot masquerade as a capability timeout.
            for stream, buffer, label in ((child.stdout, output, "stdout"),
                                          (child.stderr, diagnostic, "stderr")):
                if label in eof:
                    continue
                try:
                    part = os.read(stream.fileno(), min(4096, limit + 1 - len(buffer)))
                except BlockingIOError:
                    continue
                if part:
                    buffer.extend(part)
                    if len(buffer) > limit:
                        raise refused(f"exceeded its {label} bound")
                else:
                    eof.add(label)
            if observe_exit(child.pid, nohang=True) and len(eof) == 2:
                # Pin the leader until its last group signal. Descendants may
                # inherit either pipe; no reader thread or orphan pipe wait is
                # allowed to extend the original discovery deadline.
                resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
                child.wait()
                reaped = True
                if observation is not None:
                    observation(query, child.returncode, bytes(output), bytes(diagnostic))
                return child.returncode, bytes(output), bytes(diagnostic)
            time.sleep(0.01)
        raise refused("timed out")
    except CpuBridgeUnavailable:
        raise
    except (OSError, ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError) as error:
        raise refused(f"failed ({type(error).__name__}: {error})") from error
    finally:
        if child is not None:
            if not reaped:
                resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
                child.wait()
            child.stdout.close()
            child.stderr.close()

def worker_capability(cmd, observation=None):
    """Query the selected invocation through its bounded original-group owner."""
    invocation = worker_invocation(cmd)
    if invocation is None:
        return False
    prefix, args = invocation
    program = shutil.which(cmd[0])
    if not program:
        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("selected Targo capability program is unavailable")
    # The qualified front retains trust.lock selection and cache observation.
    # Never query its SDK target directly or move its prefix behind the query.
    query = [program, *prefix[1:], "--resource-capabilities", "--", *args]
    status, output, diagnostic = bounded_native_query(query, observation=observation)

    def refused(reason):
        return CpuBridgeUnavailable(
            f"selected Targo {program!r} capability discovery {reason}; "
            f"stdout={output.decode('utf-8', errors='replace')!r}; "
            f"stderr={diagnostic.decode('utf-8', errors='replace')!r}; no command was started")

    def capability_object(pairs):
        value = {}
        for key, entry in pairs:
            if key in value:
                raise ValueError("duplicate capability response field")
            value[key] = entry
        return value

    try:
        if status != 0:
            raise refused(f"exited with status {status}")
        value = json.loads(output, object_pairs_hook=capability_object)
        if (isinstance(value, dict)
                and set(value) == {"version", "cpu_workers", "supports_invocation", "runtime_refusal"}
                and type(value["version"]) is int and value["version"] == 3
                and value["cpu_workers"] is True
                and value["supports_invocation"] is True
                and isinstance(value["runtime_refusal"], str)
                and value["runtime_refusal"]):
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable(value["runtime_refusal"])
        if (not isinstance(value, dict)
                or set(value) != {"version", "cpu_workers", "supports_invocation"}
                or type(value["version"]) is not int or value["version"] != 3
                or type(value["cpu_workers"]) is not bool
                or type(value["supports_invocation"]) is not bool
                or (value["supports_invocation"] and not value["cpu_workers"])):
            raise refused("returned an invalid capability response")
        supported = value["cpu_workers"] and value["supports_invocation"]
        if len(prefix) > 1 and not supported:
            raise refused("does not support this native shim-front invocation")
        return supported
    except CpuBridgeUnavailable:
        raise
    except (OSError, ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError) as error:
        raise refused(f"failed ({type(error).__name__}: {error})") from error


def cpu_capacity_directory():
    """Use the same account database namespace as trust-build-cpu."""
    try:
        home = pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir
    except (KeyError, OSError) as error:
        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("CPU capacity account home unavailable") from error
    if not isinstance(home, str) or not os.path.isabs(home):
        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("CPU capacity account home is not absolute")
    suffix = "Library/Caches/aterm/capacity" if sys.platform == "darwin" else ".cache/aterm/capacity"
    return os.path.join(home, suffix, "build-cpu-v1")


def checked_cpu_file(directory, name, *, private=False):
    fd = os.open(name, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0), dir_fd=directory)
    try:
        meta = os.fstat(fd)
        if (not stat.S_ISREG(meta.st_mode) or meta.st_uid != os.geteuid()
                or meta.st_nlink != 1 or meta.st_mode & (0o077 if private else 0o022)):
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("CPU lease file has unsafe ownership or mode")
        named = os.stat(name, dir_fd=directory, follow_symlinks=False)
        if (named.st_dev, named.st_ino) != (meta.st_dev, meta.st_ino):
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("CPU lease file changed during observation")
        return fd
    except BaseException:
        os.close(fd)
        raise


def unsafe_directory_reason(path, meta, *, private=False):
    """Name a refused directory, what is wrong with it, and its owner's repair."""
    if not stat.S_ISDIR(meta.st_mode):
        return f"{path} is not a directory"
    if meta.st_uid != os.geteuid():
        return f"{path} is owned by uid {meta.st_uid}, not by this user (uid {os.geteuid()})"
    access, repair = ("open to", "go-rwx") if private else ("writable by", "go-w")
    return (f"{path} has mode {stat.S_IMODE(meta.st_mode):04o}, {access} its group or others; "
            f"build-slot never changes an existing directory: run chmod {repair} "
            f"{shlex.quote(path)}")


def checked_cpu_directory(path, *, private=False):
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_DIRECTORY", 0) | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
    meta = os.fstat(fd)
    if (not stat.S_ISDIR(meta.st_mode) or meta.st_uid != os.geteuid()
            or meta.st_mode & (0o077 if private else 0o022)):
        os.close(fd)
        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable(
            "CPU lease directory " + unsafe_directory_reason(path, meta, private=private))
    return fd


def observed_directory(path):
    """fstat `path` itself, never a link it names."""
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_DIRECTORY", 0) | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
    except OSError as error:
        if error.errno in (errno.ELOOP, errno.ENOTDIR):
            raise NamespaceError(f"{path} is not a directory: {error.strerror}") from error
        raise
    try:
        return os.fstat(fd)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def namespace_directory(path):
    """Make every missing component of `path` 0700, whatever the umask.

    os.makedirs applies the process umask to every directory it makes and its
    mode to the leaf only, so under umask 002 it made ~/.cache and
    ~/.cache/build-slot 0775, which checked_cpu_directory and trust-build-tree's
    admission then refuse. Each missing component is made here under umask 077
    and checked to be this user's directory with permission bits 0700. Special
    bits it did not ask for are not judged: on Linux mkdir(2) gives a directory
    made under a set-group-ID parent S_ISGID, which names the group of what is
    made in it and grants that group nothing. A directory that already
    existed is never changed: the leaf is admitted only when it is this user's
    and not writable by its group or others, and is otherwise refused with the
    chmod its owner should run.
    """
    path = os.path.abspath(path)
    missing = []
    probe = path
    while not os.path.lexists(probe):
        missing.append(probe)
        parent = os.path.dirname(probe)
        if parent == probe:
            break
        probe = parent
    for component in reversed(missing):
        # The umask is the defect: neutralize it for exactly this one creation.
        previous = os.umask(0o077)
        try:
            os.mkdir(component, 0o700)
        except FileExistsError:
            # A concurrent launcher made it first; judge it as an existing directory.
            continue
        finally:
            os.umask(previous)
        meta = observed_directory(component)
        # Owner rwx and nothing for its group or others; never the special bits.
        if meta.st_uid != os.geteuid() or (meta.st_mode & 0o777) != 0o700:
            raise NamespaceError(
                f"build-slot created {component} but found mode "
                f"{stat.S_IMODE(meta.st_mode):04o} owned by uid {meta.st_uid}, "
                f"not a directory of uid {os.geteuid()} with permission bits 0700")
    meta = observed_directory(path)
    if meta.st_uid != os.geteuid() or meta.st_mode & 0o022:
        raise NamespaceError(unsafe_directory_reason(path, meta))


def kernel_held(fd):
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        return True
    fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
    return False


def fixed_cpu_reservations(directory, cpus, slots):
    """Count live fixed reservations, never using PID liveness as authority.

    A malformed held record refuses the external launch. Native workers use
    the equivalent conservative full-host veto. Unlocked stale files count zero.
    """
    try:
        root = checked_cpu_directory(directory)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return 0
    try:
        try:
            fence = checked_cpu_file(root, "admission.lock")
        except FileNotFoundError:
            fence = None
        if fence is not None:
            try:
                if kernel_held(fence):
                    return cpus
            finally:
                os.close(fence)
        entries = [name for name in os.listdir(root) if re.fullmatch(r"slot-[0-9]+", name)]
        if len(entries) > 65536:
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("too many external CPU slot files")
        seen, total = {}, 0
        weight = max(1, (cpus + max(1, slots) - 1) // max(1, slots))
        for name in entries:
            fd = checked_cpu_file(root, name)
            try:
                if not kernel_held(fd):
                    continue
                raw = os.read(fd, 65537)
                if len(raw) > 65536:
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("external CPU record exceeds bound")
                try:
                    row = json.loads(raw)
                except (ValueError, UnicodeError) as error:
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("held external CPU record is unreadable") from error
                if not isinstance(row, dict):
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("held external CPU record is not an object")
                mode = row.get("cpu_mode")
                if "cpu_mode" not in row:
                    if (type(row.get("pid")) is not int or row["pid"] <= 0
                            or not isinstance(row.get("cmd"), str)
                            or not isinstance(row.get("cwd"), str) or not os.path.isabs(row["cwd"])
                            or type(row.get("started")) not in (int, float)
                            or not math.isfinite(row["started"]) or row["started"] < 0):
                        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("held legacy CPU record is incomplete")
                    total += cpus if int(name[5:]) >= slots else weight
                    continue
                lease = row.get("lease_id")
                budget, pool_slots = row.get("cpu_budget"), row.get("pool_slots")
                if (mode not in ("workers-v1", "fixed-v1")
                        or not isinstance(lease, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{32}", lease)
                        or type(budget) is not int or not 1 <= budget <= cpus
                        or type(pool_slots) is not int or not 1 <= pool_slots <= 65536
                        or int(name[5:]) >= pool_slots):
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("held external CPU record has invalid provenance")
                identity = (mode, budget, pool_slots)
                if lease in seen and seen[lease] != identity:
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("external CPU lease records disagree")
                if lease not in seen:
                    seen[lease] = identity
                    if mode == "fixed-v1":
                        total += budget
            finally:
                os.close(fd)
        return total
    finally:
        os.close(root)


def native_cpu_room(directory, cpus, slots):
    """Check and freeze native acquisition while judging fixed CPU room."""
    try:
        root = checked_cpu_directory(cpu_capacity_directory(), private=True)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return True
    try:
        manifest = checked_cpu_file(root, "pool", private=True)
        try:
            try:
                fcntl.flock(manifest, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            except BlockingIOError:
                return False
            raw = os.read(manifest, 65537)
            try:
                text = raw.decode("ascii")
            except UnicodeError as error:
                raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("native CPU manifest is not ASCII") from error
            lines = text.splitlines()
            if not lines or lines[0] != f"trust-build-cpu-v1 slots={cpus}" or len(lines) != cpus + 1:
                raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("native CPU manifest has incompatible capacity")
            held = 0
            for index, row in enumerate(lines[1:]):
                match = re.fullmatch(rf"slot={index} dev=([0-9]+) ino=([0-9]+)", row)
                if not match:
                    raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("native CPU manifest slot is invalid")
                fd = checked_cpu_file(root, f"slot-{index:08x}", private=True)
                try:
                    meta = os.fstat(fd)
                    if (meta.st_dev, meta.st_ino) != tuple(map(int, match.groups())):
                        raise CpuBridgeUnavailable(
                            f"native CPU slot {index} identity changed: "
                            f"expected dev={match[1]} ino={match[2]}, "
                            f"observed dev={meta.st_dev} ino={meta.st_ino}; "
                            "machine authority recovery is required")
                    held += int(kernel_held(fd))
                finally:
                    os.close(fd)
            return held + fixed_cpu_reservations(directory, cpus, slots) <= cpus
        finally:
            os.close(manifest)
    finally:
        os.close(root)


def checked_legacy_fence_file(root, name):
    fd = os.open(name, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0),
                 0o644, dir_fd=root)
    try:
        meta = os.fstat(fd)
        named = os.stat(name, dir_fd=root, follow_symlinks=False)
        if (not stat.S_ISREG(meta.st_mode) or meta.st_uid != os.geteuid()
                or meta.st_nlink != 1 or meta.st_mode & 0o022
                or (meta.st_dev, meta.st_ino) != (named.st_dev, named.st_ino)):
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("legacy CPU fence has unsafe ownership, mode or identity")
        return fd
    except BaseException:
        os.close(fd)
        raise


class EpochReservationLost(Exception):
    """A non-atomic EX-to-SH conversion lost admission; release and requeue."""


def try_legacy_fence(directory, slots, reservation=None, *, priority=False):
    """Retain SH locks that make every old launcher's EX acquisition fail.

    A FIFO winner already owns admission EX. Keep it while old slot holders
    drain, then convert that same descriptor to the ordinary inherited SH fence.
    Never open another admission descriptor against our own exclusive lease.
    """
    if reservation is None and not priority:
        queued, _, error = queued_status(directory)
        if queued or error:
            # New joins must not starve an already registered legacy waiter.
            return None
    namespace_directory(directory)
    root = checked_cpu_directory(directory)
    held = []
    try:
        names = {f"slot-{i}" for i in range(exclusive_slot_count(slots))}
        names.update(name for name in os.listdir(root) if re.fullmatch(r"slot-[0-9]+", name))
        if len(names) > 65536:
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("too many legacy CPU slot files")
        if reservation is not None:
            meta = os.fstat(reservation)
            named = os.stat("admission.lock", dir_fd=root, follow_symlinks=False)
            if (meta.st_dev, meta.st_ino) != (named.st_dev, named.st_ino):
                raise CpuBridgeUnavailable("legacy admission reservation identity changed")
        paths = sorted(names, key=lambda name: int(name[5:]))
        if reservation is None:
            paths.insert(0, "admission.lock")
        for name in paths:
            fd = checked_legacy_fence_file(root, name)
            try:
                fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                if active_adoption(os.path.join(directory, name)) is not None:
                    raise BlockingIOError()
                held.append(fd)
            except BaseException:
                os.close(fd)
                raise
        if reservation is not None:
            # flock conversion need not be atomic. Losing to an old exclusive
            # launcher must release every slot, not wait and deadlock its drain.
            try:
                fcntl.flock(reservation, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            except BlockingIOError as error:
                raise EpochReservationLost from error
            held.insert(0, reservation)
        result, held = held, []
        return result
    except BlockingIOError:
        return None
    finally:
        for fd in held:
            os.close(fd)
        os.close(root)


def slot_directory():
    """Keep cooperative machine admission stable across isolated build homes."""
    configured = os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_DIR")
    if configured:
        return os.path.realpath(configured)
    try:
        home = pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir
    except (KeyError, OSError) as error:
        raise NamespaceError("cannot resolve the Unix UID account home") from error
    if not isinstance(home, str) or not os.path.isabs(home) or not os.path.isdir(home):
        raise NamespaceError("Unix UID account home must be an existing absolute directory")
    return os.path.realpath(os.path.join(home, ".cache", "build-slot"))


def canonical_adoption_directory():
    # A different ambient HOME must not hide the same user's live leases.
    import pwd

    try:
        home = pwd.getpwuid(os.geteuid()).pw_dir
        if not isinstance(home, str) or not os.path.isabs(home):
            return None
        return os.path.join(os.path.realpath(home), ".cache", "build-slot", "adopted")
    except (KeyError, OSError):
        return None


ADOPTION_DIR = canonical_adoption_directory()


def resource_command(cmd, env):
    """Keep daemon-launched work attributable to its authenticated aterm session."""
    if not any(env.get(key) for key in ("ATERM_CHILD", "ATERM_PARENT_SESSION_ID", "ATERM_SESSION_ID", "ATERM_EDGE_TOKENS")):
        return cmd

    def unavailable(reason):
        print(f"build-slot: aterm resource attribution unavailable ({reason}); native command remains unreported",
              file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return cmd

    if "BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI" in env:
        cli = env["BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI"]
        if (not os.path.isabs(cli) or not os.path.isfile(cli)
                or not os.access(cli, os.X_OK)):
            return unavailable("explicit discovery executable unavailable")
    else:
        cli = shutil.which("aterm", path=env.get("PATH"))
    if cli is None:
        return unavailable("aterm executable absent")
    try:
        # The existing control route is safe on older clients/hosts. Never
        # discover support by invoking an unknown top-level command.
        probe = subprocess.run([cli, "ctl", "@self", "resources", "capabilities"],
                               env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True,
                               text=True, timeout=5)
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired, UnicodeError):
        return unavailable("control unavailable")
    words = probe.stdout.split()
    if probe.returncode or len(probe.stdout) > 8192 or words[:2] != ["OK", "resources"]:
        return unavailable("unsupported control protocol")
    fields = {}
    tail = words[3:] if words[2:3] == ["capabilities"] else words[2:]
    for word in tail:
        key, sep, value = word.partition("=")
        if not sep or key in fields:
            return unavailable("malformed capability record")
        fields[key] = value
    if fields.get("version") != "1":
        return unavailable("unsupported resource version")
    if fields.get("available", "1") != "1":
        return unavailable("host resource reporting unavailable")
    encoded = fields.get("runner", "")
    if re.search(r"%(?![0-9a-fA-F]{2})", encoded):
        return unavailable("malformed runner path")
    runner = os.fsdecode(unquote_to_bytes(encoded))
    if "\0" in runner or not os.path.isabs(runner) or not os.path.isfile(runner) or not os.access(runner, os.X_OK):
        return unavailable("runner unavailable")
    # Resolve @self through aterm's authenticated control context: inherited
    # session-id strings can be stale after adoption or a live app handoff.
    print("build-slot: routing admitted job through aterm resource-run", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    return [runner, "resource-run", "--session", "@self", "--job", job_label(cmd), "--", *cmd]


def job_label(cmd):
    """Display metadata for aterm: no command arguments, which may carry credentials."""
    label = f"{os.path.basename(os.getcwd()) or '/'}: {os.path.basename(cmd[0])}"
    # Native paths may contain arbitrary bytes or controls, and both basenames
    # can exceed the host's 200-byte UTF-8 label limit. Normalize only display
    # metadata; the exact command keeps every original argument.
    label = "".join(char if char.isprintable() else "?" for char in label).strip()
    return label.encode("utf-8")[:200].decode("utf-8", errors="ignore")


def ledger_discovery(env):
    """The aterm whose capacity ledger admits fresh work here.

    Found as resource_command finds aterm, but in or outside an aterm session:
    the ledger is the account's, and the targo builds a job starts claim in it
    wherever they run. Only two answers select the slot pool (LedgerUnavailable):
    no aterm at all, and an aterm without the verb, which refuses `claim` as an
    unknown verb with exit 2 and acts on nothing. Every other answer (a timeout,
    another exit, another reply) leaves the authority unknown (LedgerRefused):
    under load the authority must not change from one call to the next.
    """
    if "BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI" in env:
        cli = env["BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI"]
        if not os.path.isabs(cli):
            raise LedgerRefused("BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI is not an absolute path")
        if not os.path.lexists(cli):
            raise LedgerUnavailable("BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI names no file: no aterm")
        if not os.path.isfile(cli) or not os.access(cli, os.X_OK):
            raise LedgerRefused("BUILD_SLOT_ATERM_CLI is not an executable file")
    else:
        cli = shutil.which("aterm", path=env.get("PATH"))
        if cli is None:
            raise LedgerUnavailable("aterm executable absent")
    try:
        status, output, _ = bounded_native_query(
            [cli, "pkg", "claim", "--capabilities"], timeout=LEDGER_PROBE_SECONDS, limit=4096,
            purpose="capacity ledger discovery")
    except CpuBridgeUnavailable as error:
        raise LedgerRefused(f"`aterm pkg claim --capabilities` did not answer: {error}") from error
    if status == 2:
        raise LedgerUnavailable(f"`aterm pkg claim --capabilities` exited 2: "
                                f"this aterm lacks {LEDGER_CLAIM_PROTOCOL}")
    expected = LEDGER_CLAIM_PROTOCOL.encode()
    if status != 0 or output not in (expected, expected + b"\n"):
        raise LedgerRefused(f"`aterm pkg claim --capabilities` exited {status} and answered "
                            f"{output[:80].decode('utf-8', errors='replace')!r}, "
                            f"not {LEDGER_CLAIM_PROTOCOL}")
    return cli


def admission_ledger():
    """The ledger CLI for a fresh admission; None after one stderr line; LedgerRefused propagates."""
    try:
        return ledger_discovery(os.environ)
    except LedgerUnavailable as missing:
        print(f"build-slot: aterm capacity ledger unavailable ({missing}); "
              "admitting through the build-slot pool", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        return None


def print_admission_authority():
    """`status`'s last line: which authority admits a fresh build-slot command here."""
    try:
        ledger = ledger_discovery(os.environ)
    except LedgerUnavailable as missing:
        print(f"admission: fresh commands take this pool (aterm capacity ledger unavailable: {missing})")
        return
    except (LedgerRefused, NamespaceError) as unknown:
        print(f"admission: unknown, so fresh commands are refused ({unknown})")
        return
    if ledger is None:
        print("admission: fresh commands take this pool")
    else:
        print("admission: fresh commands claim in aterm's capacity ledger; `aterm pkg capacity` "
              "shows them. Slots here are held only by older build-slot copies, adopted jobs "
              "and native slot users, which that ledger counts as held cores")


def checkout_directory():
    """The worktree a claim builds in, for the ledger's view and memory book."""
    try:
        top = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, timeout=10, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, UnicodeError):
        return os.getcwd()
    path = top.stdout.strip()
    return os.path.realpath(path) if top.returncode == 0 and os.path.isabs(path) else os.getcwd()


def default_claim_key(cmd, checkout):
    """One stable book key per program and checkout, never per argument list.

    aterm sizes a claim that names no memory from the measured peak booked under
    its key. A key that changed with every argv would never gather that history,
    and every such claim would stay at the ledger's cold figure.
    """
    digest = hashlib.sha256(os.fsencode(checkout)).hexdigest()
    name = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._+-]", "_", os.path.basename(cmd[0]))[:64] or "command"
    return f"build-slot:{name}:{digest[:16]}"


def ledger_argv(cli, *, label, key, checkout, rank, memory_bytes, cores, alone,
                worktree_fd, wait_ms, once, since_ms, status_fd):
    """The verb's words for one covering claim; the command follows its `--`."""
    argv = [cli, "pkg", "claim", "--what", label, "--key", key, "--checkout", checkout,
            "--rank", rank, "--cores", str(cores)]
    if memory_bytes is not None:
        argv += ["--mem-bytes", str(memory_bytes)]
    if alone:
        # No other claim or held pool slot beside it; build-slot's own quiet
        # wait then runs under the claim before the command (ledger_quiet_exec).
        argv.append("--alone")
    if worktree_fd is not None:
        # The worktree lock is taken in the same look that admits, never held
        # while the claim waits, and kept by the command across its exec.
        argv += ["--flock-fd", str(worktree_fd)]
    if once:
        argv.append("--no-wait")
        if since_ms is not None:
            argv += ["--since-ms", str(since_ms)]
    elif wait_ms is not None:
        argv += ["--wait-ms", str(wait_ms)]
    return [*argv, "--status-fd", str(status_fd), "--"]


def ledger_event(raw, cores):
    """The verb's one admission record; anything else is a protocol refusal."""
    record = decode_admission_record(raw)
    event = record.get("event")
    keys = ({"v", "event", "cores", "mem_bytes", "rank", "marker"} if event == "admitted"
            else {"v", "event", "cores", "marker"} if event == "covered" else None)
    if keys is None or set(record) != keys:
        raise ValueError("not an admitted or covered record")
    if type(record["v"]) is not int or record["v"] != 1:
        raise ValueError("unsupported record version")
    if type(record["cores"]) is not int or not 1 <= record["cores"] <= cores:
        raise ValueError(f"grant {record['cores']!r} is not 1 to the {cores} cores asked for")
    if not isinstance(record["marker"], str) or not record["marker"]:
        raise ValueError("no cover marker")
    if event == "admitted" and (type(record["mem_bytes"]) is not int or record["mem_bytes"] < 0
                                or record["rank"] not in RANKS):
        raise ValueError("invalid memory or rank")
    return record


def wait_until_quiet(mem_gib, check_deadline, wait, say):
    """Exclusive admission's host readiness: measured memory, a quiet load and no compiler
    for QUIET_SECONDS. The pool runs it holding every slot; the ledger under its ALONE claim."""
    quiet_since = None
    while True:
        check_deadline()
        avail, load, builds = available_gib(), load1(), build_processes()
        reason = None
        if avail is None or not math.isfinite(avail) or avail < mem_gib:
            reason = ("mem", f"memory {avail} GiB unavailable or below {mem_gib:g} GiB")
        elif not math.isfinite(load) or load < 0 or load > QUIET_LOAD_FRACTION * NCPU:
            reason = ("load", f"load1 {load:g} unavailable or above {QUIET_LOAD_FRACTION:g} * {NCPU} CPUs")
        elif builds is None or builds:
            reason = ("processes", f"build/compiler processes: {builds}")
        if reason:
            quiet_since = None
            key, message = reason
            say(key, f"waiting: {message}")
        else:
            now = time.monotonic()
            if quiet_since is None:
                quiet_since = now
            if now - quiet_since >= QUIET_SECONDS:
                print(f"build-slot: quiet for {QUIET_SECONDS:g}s: load1={load:g} cpus={NCPU} avail_gib={avail:.1f} build_processes=0", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
                return
        wait(2)


def ledger_quiet_exec(args):
    """`--_ledger-quiet MEM_GIB DEADLINE [--execution-start-fd N] -- COMMAND...`.

    What the verb execs for --exclusive, in the claim's own PID and under its
    ALONE claim: build-slot's quiet-machine wait, then COMMAND in this PID. A
    DEADLINE of 0 is none; otherwise it is the wall-clock end of --wait-timeout,
    and passing it starts nothing (exit 2, as the pool's timeout).
    """
    try:
        split = args.index("--")
        words, command = args[:split], args[split + 1:]
        mem_gib, deadline = float(words[0]), float(words[1])
        rest = words[2:]
        start = None
        if rest[:1] == ["--execution-start-fd"] and len(rest) == 2:
            start = ExecutionStart(rest[1])
        elif rest:
            raise ValueError
        if not command or not math.isfinite(mem_gib) or not math.isfinite(deadline):
            raise ValueError
    except (ValueError, IndexError):
        print("build-slot: REFUSED — malformed ledger quiet entry; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    announced = set()

    def say(key, message):
        if key not in announced:
            announced.add(key)
            print(f"build-slot: {message}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)

    def check_deadline():
        if deadline and time.time() >= deadline:
            raise AdmissionTimeout

    def wait(seconds):
        check_deadline()
        time.sleep(seconds if not deadline else max(0.0, min(seconds, deadline - time.time())))

    wait_until_quiet(mem_gib, check_deadline, wait, say)
    if start is not None:
        start.notify(os.getpid(), time.clock_gettime_ns(time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC) // 1000)
    os.execvp(command[0], command)


def stop_unanswered_claim(child, observe_exit):
    """TERM the verb's group, KILL it after LEDGER_STOP_GRACE; leave it unreaped."""
    owner = resource_transport_owner()
    owner.signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGTERM)
    stop_by = time.monotonic() + LEDGER_STOP_GRACE
    while not observe_exit(child.pid, nohang=True):
        if time.monotonic() >= stop_by:
            owner.signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
            observe_exit(child.pid)
            break
        time.sleep(0.05)


def ledger_admit_and_run(cli, cmd, owned, *, legacy_dir, cores, mem_gib, mem_explicit, exclusive,
                         per_worktree, wait_timeout, memory_attempt, memory_since_ms,
                         execution_start, rank, claim_key):
    """One ledger claim covers the whole command; build-slot itself holds no capacity.

    `aterm pkg claim` waits holding nothing, takes the per-worktree lock in the
    look that admits, writes one record to a private status pipe and execs the
    command in its own PID, through resource-run when that attributes it to an
    aterm session. While it waits it watches that pipe: if build-slot dies, the
    reader closes and the waiter leaves the ledger. build-slot bounds the wait
    itself as well, so a verb that never answers cannot hold this caller.
    """
    deadline = time.monotonic() + wait_timeout if wait_timeout is not None else None
    if not math.isfinite(mem_gib) or not 0 <= mem_gib < 2**33:
        print("build-slot: REFUSED — --mem-gb must be finite and nonnegative; no command was started",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    own_args = cmd[1:cmd.index("--", 1)] if "--" in cmd[1:] else cmd[1:]
    if os.path.basename(cmd[0]) in ("targo", "atpkg") and "--resource-worker-v2" in own_args:
        print("build-slot: REFUSED — native worker epochs are granted only by the build-slot pool, "
              "and this host admits through aterm's capacity ledger; no command was started",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    observe_exit = original_child_exit_observer()
    if observe_exit is None:
        return 2
    worktree = worktree_lock_path() if per_worktree else None
    worktree_fd = None
    if worktree:
        # An adopted job holds its worktree by record, not by flock: wait it
        # out holding nothing, as the pool's try_lease does.
        announced = False
        while (holder := worktree_holder(worktree)) is not None:
            kind, info = holder
            if memory_attempt is not None:
                return 75  # heavy_gate releases its memory and retries this attempt
            if not announced:
                print(f"build-slot: waiting: another build-slot job runs in this worktree "
                      f"(pid={info.get('pid')} cmd={info.get('cmd')})", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
                announced = True
            if kind == "flock":
                break  # the verb takes the lock in the look that admits
            if deadline is not None and time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                raise AdmissionTimeout
            time.sleep(2 if deadline is None else max(0.0, min(2, deadline - time.monotonic())))
        worktree_fd = os.open(worktree, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
        owned.add(worktree_fd)
    wait_ms = None
    if deadline is not None:
        wait_ms = math.ceil((deadline - time.monotonic()) * 1000)
        if wait_ms <= 0:
            raise AdmissionTimeout
    checkout = checkout_directory()
    key = claim_key or default_claim_key(cmd, checkout)
    # A claim names its memory only where the caller did; otherwise the ledger
    # sizes it from the key's measured peak, or its own cold figure.
    memory_bytes = math.ceil(mem_gib * 1073741824) if mem_explicit else None
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["BUILD_SLOT_HELD"] = "1"
    env["BUILD_SLOT_DIR"] = legacy_dir
    env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_EXCLUSIVE", None)
    if exclusive:
        env["BUILD_SLOT_EXCLUSIVE"] = "1"
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_PROTOCOL"] = "1"
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_SOURCE"] = "ledger-grant"
    # The asked-for cores bound the command even before the verb lowers all
    # three to its grant at exec: targo reads TARGO_CALLER_JOBS as a hard cap.
    for name in ("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS", "TARGO_PLANNED_JOBS", "TARGO_CALLER_JOBS"):
        env[name] = str(cores)
    for name in ("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_BUDGET", "BUILD_SLOT_CPU_MODE", "BUILD_SLOT_POOL_SLOTS",
                 "BUILD_SLOT_LEGACY_DIR", "BUILD_SLOT_V2_DIR", "BUILD_SLOT_V2_SLOTS",
                 "BUILD_SLOT_FENCE_FDS"):
        env.pop(name, None)
    launch = resource_command(cmd, env)
    passed = {*inherited_resource_fds(env)}
    if worktree_fd is not None:
        passed.add(worktree_fd)
    quiet_start = None
    if exclusive:
        # The ALONE claim drains the ledger and the pool; the quiet wait that
        # the pool runs holding every slot runs here under that claim.
        quiet = [*(_REEXEC or [sys.executable, "-I", "-B", os.path.abspath(__file__)]),
                 "--_ledger-quiet", repr(mem_gib),
                 repr(time.time() + (deadline - time.monotonic())) if deadline is not None else "0"]
        if execution_start is not None:
            quiet_start, execution_start = execution_start, None
            quiet += ["--execution-start-fd", str(quiet_start.fd)]
            passed.add(quiet_start.fd)
        launch = [*quiet, "--", *launch]
    reader, writer = os.pipe()
    owned.add(reader)
    claim = ledger_argv(cli, label=job_label(cmd), key=key, checkout=checkout, rank=rank,
                        memory_bytes=memory_bytes, cores=cores, alone=exclusive,
                        worktree_fd=worktree_fd, wait_ms=wait_ms, once=memory_attempt is not None,
                        since_ms=memory_since_ms, status_fd=writer)
    print(f"build-slot: claiming in aterm's capacity ledger: key={key} rank={rank} cores<={cores} "
          f"mem_bytes={'by key' if memory_bytes is None else memory_bytes}{' alone' if exclusive else ''}",
          file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
    try:
        child = subprocess.Popen([*claim, *launch], env=env, start_new_session=True,
                                 pass_fds=sorted({writer, *passed}))
    finally:
        os.close(writer)
        if quiet_start is not None:
            os.close(quiet_start.fd)  # the quiet entry alone reports the start
    interrupted = None
    forwardable = child

    def forward(sig, _frame):
        nonlocal interrupted
        interrupted = sig
        if forwardable is not None:
            resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(forwardable.pid, sig)

    previous = {sig: signal.signal(sig, forward)
                for sig in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP)}
    record, refusal, notification_failed, unanswered = None, None, False, False
    answer_by = None if deadline is None else deadline + LEDGER_ANSWER_GRACE
    try:
        raw = b""
        while b"\n" not in raw and len(raw) <= 4096:
            if answer_by is not None:
                remaining = answer_by - time.monotonic()
                if remaining <= 0 or not select.select([reader], [], [], remaining)[0]:
                    if time.monotonic() < answer_by:
                        continue
                    # The verb outlived its --wait-ms and the grace: stop it.
                    unanswered = True
                    stop_unanswered_claim(child, observe_exit)
                    os.set_blocking(reader, False)
                    try:
                        raw += os.read(reader, 4097 - len(raw))
                    except BlockingIOError:
                        pass
                    break
            part = os.read(reader, 4097 - len(raw))
            if not part:
                break
            raw += part
        started_us = time.clock_gettime_ns(time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC) // 1000
        if raw:
            try:
                if not raw.endswith(b"\n") or raw.count(b"\n") != 1:
                    raise ValueError("not one newline-terminated record")
                record = ledger_event(raw, cores)
            except (ValueError, UnicodeError, RecursionError) as error:
                refusal = f"aterm pkg claim sent an invalid admission record ({error}); its command was stopped"
                resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        if record is not None and unanswered:
            refusal = ("aterm pkg claim admitted the command only after its wait bound; "
                       "its command was stopped")
        elif record is not None:
            print(f"build-slot: aterm {record['event']} the command with {record['cores']} cores",
                  file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
            if worktree_fd is not None:
                os.ftruncate(worktree_fd, 0)
                os.write(worktree_fd, json.dumps({"pid": child.pid, "cmd": job_label(cmd), "cwd": os.getcwd(),
                                                  "started": time.time(), "ledger": True}).encode())
            if memory_attempt is not None:
                os.write(memory_attempt, b"R")
                os.close(memory_attempt)
            if execution_start is not None:
                try:
                    execution_start.notify(child.pid, started_us)
                except Exception as error:
                    # The original child/group still belongs to us. A closed
                    # receiver must not strand it or retire its claim early.
                    notification_failed = True
                    print(f"build-slot: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
                    resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        observe_exit(child.pid)
        forwardable = None
        rc = child.wait()
    finally:
        forwardable = None
        for sig, handler in previous.items():
            signal.signal(sig, handler)
    if refusal is not None:
        print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — {refusal}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if record is None:
        # The verb starts the command only after its admission record.
        if interrupted is not None:
            return 128 + interrupted
        if unanswered:
            raise AdmissionTimeout
        if memory_attempt is not None and rc == 75:
            return 75  # one look found no room: heavy_gate releases memory and retries
        why = ("its wait ended without admission" if rc == 75
               else f"`aterm pkg claim` exited {128 - rc if rc < 0 else rc} without admitting")
        print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — aterm's capacity ledger did not admit this command: {why}; "
              "no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    return 2 if notification_failed else (128 - rc if rc < 0 else rc)


def worktree_holder(path):
    """Who holds the worktree now, judged as try_lease judges it, holding nothing after.

    ("flock", stamp) for a live lock holder, ("adopted", record) for an adopted
    job (checked under the flock, as active_adoption requires), else None. The
    verb takes the flock itself in the look that admits, so a flock answer only
    names the holder and lets heavy_gate's attempt retry early.
    """
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
    try:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            return "flock", holder_info(path) or {}
        adopted = active_adoption(path)
        return None if adopted is None else ("adopted", adopted)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def cpu_jobs(slots, requested=None, *, budget=None, strict=False):
    """A caller may use less than its slot's CPU share, never more."""
    if slots < 1:
        raise ValueError("--slots must be positive")
    share = max(1, NCPU // slots) if budget is None else budget
    if requested is None:
        return share
    # Keep the existing oversized-input refusal on Python versions without
    # the integer-conversion digit limit, and do not depend on its setting.
    if len(requested) > 4300:
        raise ValueError("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS is too large to parse")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", requested):
        raise ValueError("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS must be a positive integer")
    try:
        jobs = int(requested)
    except ValueError:
        raise ValueError("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS is too large to parse") from None
    if jobs < 1:
        raise ValueError("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS must be a positive integer")
    if strict and jobs > share:
        raise ValueError("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS must be no larger than --cpus")
    return min(share, jobs)


def job_provenance(env, cpus=None):
    """Separate generated counts from immutable caller upper bounds."""
    raw = env.get("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS")
    positive = lambda value: (isinstance(value, str) and len(value) <= 4300
                              and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", value) and int(value) > 0)
    generated = positive(raw) and (
        raw == env.get("TARGO_PLANNED_JOBS")
        or (env.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_SOURCE") == "available-slots"
            and raw == env.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_BUDGET")))
    caps = []
    caller = env.get("TARGO_CALLER_JOBS")
    if caller:
        if not positive(caller):
            raise ValueError("TARGO_CALLER_JOBS must be a positive integer")
        caps.append(int(caller))
    if raw is not None and not generated:
        cpu_jobs(1, raw)  # retain the existing strict numeric validation
        caps.append(int(raw))
    if cpus is not None:
        caps.append(cpus)
    return bool(generated), min(caps) if caps else None


def default_slots():
    env = os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOTS")
    if env and env.isdigit() and int(env) > 0:
        return int(env)
    return max(1, NCPU // 6)


def exclusive_slot_count(slots):
    # --slots 1 alone cannot exclude default workers, which also use slot-1,
    # slot-2, ... . Cover the host default and the configured/requested pool.
    return max(1, NCPU // 6, default_slots(), slots)


def try_exclusive_slots(slots):
    """Acquire the whole pool, or release every partial lock before waiting."""
    acquired = []
    try:
        for i in pool_slots(slots):
            path = os.path.join(DIR, f"slot-{i}")
            fd = try_lease(path)
            if fd is None:
                raise BlockingIOError()
            acquired.append((i, fd, path))
    except BaseException as error:
        for _, fd, _ in acquired:
            os.close(fd)
        if isinstance(error, BlockingIOError):
            return None
        raise
    return acquired


def try_shared_slots(slots, needed, maximum=None, reserved=0):
    """Acquire actual leases; optional borrowing leaves pending minimum claims."""
    acquired = []
    limit = maximum or needed
    try:
        for i in range(slots):
            path = os.path.join(DIR, f"slot-{i}")
            fd = try_lease(path)
            if fd is not None:
                acquired.append((i, fd, path))
                if not reserved and len(acquired) == limit:
                    break
        if len(acquired) < needed:
            return None
        # Count the actually free, exclusively held descriptions, not nominal
        # pool width. Busy slots cannot also back a pending peer's reservation.
        keep = min(limit, max(needed, len(acquired) - reserved))
        while len(acquired) > keep:
            _, fd, _ = acquired.pop()
            os.close(fd)
        result, acquired = acquired, []
        return result
    finally:
        for _, fd, _ in acquired:
            os.close(fd)


class NativeMemoryObservation(float):
    """One fresh native kernel reading; its GiB projection is diagnostic."""
    def __new__(cls, count):
        if type(count) is not int or not 0 <= count < 2**64:
            raise ValueError("invalid native available-memory bytes")
        value = super().__new__(cls, count / 1073741824)
        value.native_bytes = count
        return value


def native_memory_observation():
    """Use the selected maintained observer, never a program named by a ticket."""
    program = shutil.which("trust-build-status")
    arguments = ["--json"]
    if not program:
        program = shutil.which("targo")
        arguments = ["--unverified", "resource", "status", "--json"]
    if not program:
        return None
    try:
        status, output, _ = bounded_native_query(
            [program, *arguments],
            timeout=2, limit=65536, purpose="memory observation")
        if status:
            return None
        record = decode_admission_record(output)
        if record.get("protocol") != "native-resource-status-v1":
            return None
        return NativeMemoryObservation(record["available_memory_bytes"])
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OverflowError, RecursionError,
            subprocess.SubprocessError, NamespaceError, CpuBridgeUnavailable):
        return None


def available_gib():
    """Available memory in GiB, or None if it cannot be measured."""
    native = native_memory_observation()
    if native is not None:
        return native
    try:
        if sys.platform == "darwin":
            out = subprocess.run(["vm_stat"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10).stdout
            page = 4096
            first = out.splitlines()[0] if out else ""
            if "page size of" in first:
                page = int(first.split("page size of")[1].split()[0])
            pages = 0
            for line in out.splitlines():
                key, _, val = line.partition(":")
                if key.strip() in ("Pages free", "Pages inactive", "Pages purgeable", "Pages speculative"):
                    pages += int(val.strip().rstrip("."))
            return pages * page / 2**30
        with open("/proc/meminfo") as f:
            for line in f:
                if line.startswith("MemAvailable:"):
                    return int(line.split()[1]) / 2**20
    except Exception:
        return None
    return None


def load1():
    try:
        return os.getloadavg()[0]
    except OSError:
        return -1.0


def build_processes():
    """Conservative exact-name readiness probe; unknown is never quiet."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-axo", "pid=,stat=,comm="],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10, check=True).stdout
        lines = out.splitlines()
        if not lines or len(lines) > 1_000_000:
            return None
        found = []
        for line in lines:
            parts = line.split(None, 2)
            if len(parts) != 3 or not parts[0].isdigit():
                return None
            pid, state, comm = parts
            if not state.startswith("Z") and os.path.basename(comm) in {"cargo", "targo", "rustc", "trustc"}:
                found.append((int(pid), comm))
        return found
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, UnicodeError):
        return None



def pool_slots(slots):
    """Include historic larger pools without inventing gaps up to a stale index."""
    return sorted(set(range(exclusive_slot_count(slots))) | {
        int(name[5:]) for name in os.listdir(DIR)
        if re.fullmatch(r"slot-[0-9]+", name)
    })



def worktree_lock_path():
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--absolute-git-dir"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except Exception:
        return None
    gd = r.stdout.strip()
    return os.path.join(gd, "build-slot.lock") if r.returncode == 0 and gd else None


def holder_info(path):
    adopted = read_adoption(path)
    if adopted is not None:
        return adopted
    try:
        with open(path) as f:
            return json.loads(f.read() or "{}")
    except Exception:
        return {}


def alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(int(pid), 0)
        return True
    except Exception:
        return False


class IdentityError(Exception):
    """A native query could not establish a stable process identity."""


def confirmed_absent(pid):
    # Missing procfs/libproc data may mean hidden or inaccessible, not dead.
    # Signal zero is only a kernel existence probe; it sends no signal.
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return True
    except OSError:
        pass
    return False


def process_identity(pid):
    """No argv/environment query; birth distinguishes PID reuse, including exec."""
    try:
        if sys.platform == "darwin":
            import ctypes
            import errno

            class BsdInfo(ctypes.Structure):
                _fields_ = [("ids", ctypes.c_uint32 * 12), ("comm", ctypes.c_char * 16),
                            ("name", ctypes.c_char * 32), ("tail", ctypes.c_uint32 * 6),
                            ("seconds", ctypes.c_uint64), ("micros", ctypes.c_uint64)]

            lib = ctypes.CDLL("/usr/lib/libproc.dylib", use_errno=True)
            lib.proc_pidinfo.argtypes = [ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_uint64,
                                        ctypes.c_void_p, ctypes.c_int]
            lib.proc_pidpath.argtypes = [ctypes.c_int, ctypes.c_void_p, ctypes.c_uint32]

            def snapshot():
                info = BsdInfo()
                ctypes.set_errno(0)
                size = lib.proc_pidinfo(pid, 3, 0, ctypes.byref(info), ctypes.sizeof(info))
                if size == 0 and ctypes.get_errno() == errno.ESRCH:
                    if confirmed_absent(pid):
                        return None
                    raise IdentityError("native identity is unavailable for an existing process")
                if size != ctypes.sizeof(info) or info.ids[3] != pid:
                    raise IdentityError("native process birth query failed")
                if info.ids[1] == 5:  # SZOMB: the direct command has exited.
                    return None
                return info.ids[5], f"darwin:{info.seconds}:{info.micros}"

            before = snapshot()
            if before is None:
                return None
            path = ctypes.create_string_buffer(4096)
            if lib.proc_pidpath(pid, path, len(path)) <= 0:
                raise IdentityError("native executable query failed")
            executable = os.fsdecode(path.value)
            if snapshot() != before:
                raise IdentityError("process changed during its identity query")
            return {"pid": pid, "uid": before[0], "birth": before[1], "executable": executable}
        if sys.platform.startswith("linux"):
            prefix = f"/proc/{pid}"

            def snapshot():
                try:
                    with open(prefix + "/stat") as stream:
                        stat = stream.read(4096)
                    with open(prefix + "/status") as stream:
                        status = stream.read(16384)
                except FileNotFoundError:
                    if confirmed_absent(pid):
                        return None
                    raise IdentityError("procfs identity is unavailable for an existing process")
                fields = stat.rpartition(")")[2].split()
                if fields[0] == "Z":
                    return None
                uid = next(line.split()[2] for line in status.splitlines() if line.startswith("Uid:"))
                return int(uid), fields[19]

            before = snapshot()
            if before is None:
                return None
            executable = os.readlink(prefix + "/exe")
            with open("/proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id") as stream:
                boot = stream.read(128).strip()
            if not boot or snapshot() != before:
                raise IdentityError("process changed during its identity query")
            return {"pid": pid, "uid": before[0], "birth": f"linux:{boot}:{before[1]}",
                    "executable": executable}
        raise IdentityError("native process identity is unsupported on this host")
    except IdentityError:
        raise
    except Exception as error:
        raise IdentityError(f"native process identity is unavailable ({type(error).__name__})") from error


def process_cwd(pid):
    try:
        if sys.platform.startswith("linux"):
            return os.readlink(f"/proc/{pid}/cwd")
        if sys.platform == "darwin":
            result = subprocess.run(
                ["/usr/sbin/lsof", "-nP", "-a", "-p", str(pid), "-d", "cwd", "-F0n"],
                capture_output=True, timeout=10,
            )
            paths = [field[1:] for raw in result.stdout.split(b"\0")
                     if (field := raw.lstrip(b"\n")).startswith(b"n")]
            if result.returncode == 0 and len(paths) == 1:
                return os.fsdecode(paths[0])
        raise IdentityError("native working-directory query failed")
    except IdentityError:
        raise
    except Exception as error:
        raise IdentityError("native working-directory query is unavailable") from error


def same_process(left, right):
    # An exec or UID change is not PID reuse: keep that process accounted for.
    return left.get("pid") == right.get("pid") and left.get("birth") == right.get("birth")


def adoption_records():
    if ADOPTION_DIR is None:
        return [(None, {"adopted": True, "pid": None,
                        "cmd": "canonical user home unavailable; held fail-closed"})]
    try:
        names = sorted(name for name in os.listdir(ADOPTION_DIR) if name.endswith(".json"))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return []
    except Exception:
        return [(None, {"adopted": True, "pid": None, "cmd": "unreadable adoption registry; held fail-closed"})]
    records = []
    for name in names:
        record = os.path.join(ADOPTION_DIR, name)
        try:
            with open(record) as stream:
                info = json.load(stream)
            identity = info["identity"]
            valid = (info.get("adopted") is True and type(info.get("schema")) is int
                     and info["schema"] == 1
                     and type(identity.get("pid")) is int and identity["pid"] > 0
                     and info.get("pid") == identity["pid"]
                     and type(identity.get("uid")) is int
                     and isinstance(identity.get("birth"), str) and identity["birth"]
                     and isinstance(identity.get("executable"), str) and identity["executable"]
                     and isinstance(info.get("leases"), list) and info["leases"]
                     and all(isinstance(path, str) and os.path.isabs(path)
                             and os.path.realpath(path) == path for path in info["leases"])
                     and isinstance(info.get("pool"), str) and os.path.isabs(info["pool"])
                     and (info.get("worktree") is None or info["worktree"] in info["leases"]))
            if not valid:
                raise ValueError("invalid adopted lease")
            records.append((record, info))
        except FileNotFoundError:
            continue  # Another acquirer reclaimed this already-dead identity.
        except Exception:
            records.append((record, {"adopted": True, "pid": None,
                                     "cmd": "unreadable adopted lease; held fail-closed"}))
    return records


def read_adoption(path):
    path = os.path.realpath(path)
    for _, info in adoption_records():
        if "identity" not in info or path in info["leases"]:
            return info
    return None


def active_adoption(path):
    # Call only while holding this path's flock. Publication owns every path
    # before making its one full record visible, even across different pools.
    path = os.path.realpath(path)
    for record, info in adoption_records():
        if "identity" not in info:
            return info
        if path not in info["leases"]:
            continue
        try:
            current = process_identity(info["identity"]["pid"])
        except IdentityError:
            return info
        if current is not None and same_process(current, info["identity"]):
            return info
        try:
            os.unlink(record)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
    return None


def try_lease(path):
    """Test virtual adoption only under the same flock used by every writer."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        info = active_adoption(path)
        if info is not None:
            os.close(fd)
            return None
        return fd
    except BlockingIOError:
        os.close(fd)
        return None
    except BaseException:
        os.close(fd)
        raise


@contextmanager
def admission_registry():
    """Serialize ticket registration/retirement, never the admitted command."""
    directory = os.path.join(os.path.realpath(DIR), "admission")
    namespace_directory(directory)
    fd = os.open(os.path.join(directory, "registry.lock"), os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        yield directory
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def same_waiter_file(fd, path):
    held = os.fstat(fd)
    found = os.stat(path, follow_symlinks=False)
    return (held.st_dev, held.st_ino) == (found.st_dev, found.st_ino)


def next_admission_order(directory, live):
    """Reserve an arrival even when its memory wait has no live CPU ticket.

    The registry lock is held. A counter also avoids comparing per-process
    monotonic epochs on older macOS Python interpreters.
    """
    path = os.path.join(directory, "sequence")
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        previous = 0
    else:
        try:
            meta = os.fstat(fd)
            raw = os.read(fd, 64)
            if (not stat.S_ISREG(meta.st_mode) or meta.st_uid != os.geteuid()
                    or meta.st_nlink != 1 or meta.st_mode & 0o022
                    or not raw.strip().isdigit() or len(raw.strip()) > 39):
                raise NamespaceError("unsafe admission sequence")
            previous = int(raw)
        finally:
            os.close(fd)
    order = max(previous, max(live, default=0)) + 1
    temporary = path + "." + secrets.token_hex(8)
    fd = os.open(temporary, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, str(order).encode())
        os.close(fd)
        fd = None
        os.replace(temporary, path)
    finally:
        if fd is not None:
            os.close(fd)
        try:
            os.unlink(temporary)
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
    return order


def try_resources(worktree, slots, exclusive, needed=1):
    """Acquire the whole claim or release it; called under admission registry."""
    leases = []
    try:
        if worktree:
            fd = try_lease(worktree)
            if fd is None:
                raise BlockingIOError("worktree")
            leases.append((worktree, fd))
        if exclusive:
            acquired = try_exclusive_slots(slots)
            if not acquired:
                raise BlockingIOError("slots")
            leases.extend((path, fd) for _, fd, path in acquired)
        else:
            acquired = try_shared_slots(slots, needed)
            if not acquired:
                raise BlockingIOError("slots")
            leases.extend((path, fd) for _, fd, path in acquired)
        result, leases = leases, []
        return result
    finally:
        for _, fd in leases:
            os.close(fd)


def try_command_claim(worktree, slots, exclusive, needed, maximum=None, pending=None):
    """Claim under the queue lock, without waiting while holding partial leases.

    The oldest eligible exclusive command reserves admission and its worktree
    before draining old slot holders. Keep the existing admission.lock protocol
    so commands already using that protocol cannot enter during its quiet check.
    """
    leases = []
    try:
        if worktree:
            fd = try_lease(worktree)
            if fd is None:
                raise BlockingIOError("worktree")
            leases.append((worktree, fd))
        path = os.path.join(DIR, "admission.lock")
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, (fcntl.LOCK_EX if exclusive else fcntl.LOCK_SH) | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            os.close(fd)
            raise BlockingIOError("admission")
        leases.append((path, fd))
        if not exclusive:
            # Take the actual minimum first, under the same queue/worktree/
            # admission custody. Only peers that can run beside this minimum
            # may withhold optional shares; nominal free width is insufficient.
            elastic = pending is not None and maximum and maximum > needed
            acquired = try_shared_slots(slots, needed, None if elastic else maximum)
            if not acquired:
                raise BlockingIOError("slots")
            leases.extend((path, fd) for _, fd, path in acquired)
            if elastic:
                reserved, protected = pending()
                try:
                    extra = try_shared_slots(slots, 0, maximum - needed, reserved)
                    leases.extend((path, fd) for _, fd, path in extra)
                finally:
                    # These are only probes for queued minima, never child
                    # grants. Keep their exact slots free through our borrow.
                    for _, fd, _ in protected:
                        os.close(fd)
        result, leases = leases, []
        return result
    finally:
        for _, fd in leases:
            os.close(fd)


def decode_admission_record(data):
    """Read either original queue protocol without accepting ambiguous fields."""
    if len(data) > 65536:
        raise ValueError("admission ticket exceeds its bound")

    def unique(pairs):
        row = {}
        for key, value in pairs:
            if key in row:
                raise ValueError("duplicate admission field")
            row[key] = value
        return row

    def invalid_constant(value):
        raise ValueError("invalid admission JSON number")

    # serde_json reads UTF8 JSON and rejects native unsigned fields spelled
    # as -0. Preserve that token's float kind instead of Python's integer 0.
    record = json.loads(data.decode("utf-8"), object_pairs_hook=unique,
                        parse_int=lambda value: -0.0 if value == "-0" else int(value),
                        parse_constant=invalid_constant)
    if not isinstance(record, dict):
        raise ValueError("admission ticket is not an object")
    return record


def admission_requirements(record):
    """Normalize original native byte requirements and legacy GiB requirements.

    A ticket establishes queue priority only. Resource and worktree leases must
    still be acquired by their original owners. Unknown protocols stay barriers.
    """
    required = record["requires"]
    if not isinstance(required, dict):
        raise ValueError("admission requirements are not an object")
    if "native_admission_version" in record:
        if (set(record) != {"native_admission_version", "pid", "requires"}
                or type(record["native_admission_version"]) is not int
                or record["native_admission_version"] != 1
                or type(record["pid"]) is not int or not 1 <= record["pid"] < 2**32
                or not {"slots", "needed", "exclusive", "minimum_memory_bytes"} <= set(required)
                or set(required) - {"worktree_bytes", "slots", "needed", "exclusive",
                                    "minimum_memory_bytes"}):
            raise ValueError("unsupported native admission record")
        memory = required["minimum_memory_bytes"]
        if type(memory) is not int or not 0 <= memory < 2**64:
            raise ValueError("invalid native admission memory")
        path = required.get("worktree_bytes")
        if path is not None:
            if (not isinstance(path, list) or len(path) > 32768
                    or any(type(byte) is not int or not 0 <= byte <= 255 for byte in path)):
                raise ValueError("invalid native worktree bytes")
            path = bytes(path)
    else:
        if (not {"slots", "memory", "exclusive"} <= set(required)
                or set(required) - {"worktree", "slots", "memory", "exclusive", "needed"}):
            raise ValueError("invalid legacy admission requirements")
        gib = required["memory"]
        if type(gib) not in (int, float) or not math.isfinite(gib) or gib < 0:
            raise ValueError("invalid legacy admission memory")
        scaled = gib * 1073741824
        if not math.isfinite(scaled) or scaled >= 2**64:
            raise ValueError("legacy admission memory overflows")
        memory = math.ceil(scaled)
        path = required.get("worktree")
        if path is not None:
            if not isinstance(path, str):
                raise ValueError("invalid legacy worktree path")
            path.encode("utf-8")
            path = os.fsencode(path)
    if path is not None:
        if (not path.startswith(b"/") or len(path) > 32768 or b"\0" in path
                or b".." in path.split(b"/")):
            raise ValueError("invalid admission worktree path")
        path = os.fsdecode(path)
    slots, needed, exclusive = required["slots"], required.get("needed", 1), required["exclusive"]
    if (type(slots) is not int or not 1 <= slots <= 65536
            or type(needed) is not int or not 1 <= needed <= slots
            or type(exclusive) is not bool):
        raise ValueError("invalid admission slot requirements")
    return {"worktree": path, "slots": slots, "needed": needed, "exclusive": exclusive,
            "native": "native_admission_version" in record,
            "minimum_memory_bytes": memory, "memory": memory / 1073741824}


def read_admission_requirements(path):
    with open(path, "rb") as stream:
        return admission_requirements(decode_admission_record(stream.read(65537)))


def waiter_eligible(path, available, *, draining=False):
    """A busy worktree or memory-ineligible waiter does not idle other slots.

    Eligible exclusive and multi-slot requests reserve the queue while CPUs drain.
    Unreadable requirements fail closed as a barrier, never as permission to pass.
    """
    try:
        required = read_admission_requirements(path)
        worktree, slots = required["worktree"], required["slots"]
        memory, exclusive = required["minimum_memory_bytes"], required["exclusive"]
        needed = required.get("needed", 1)
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OverflowError, RecursionError):
        return True
    if required["native"] and not isinstance(available, NativeMemoryObservation):
        return True
    available_bytes = (available.native_bytes if isinstance(available, NativeMemoryObservation)
                       else available * 1073741824 if available is not None else None)
    if available_bytes is not None and available_bytes < memory:
        return False
    worktree_fd = None
    try:
        if worktree:
            worktree_fd = try_lease(worktree)
            if worktree_fd is None:
                return False
        if exclusive or draining or needed > 1:
            # An epoch join would itself extend the SH fences blocking an older
            # fixed request. Only memory/worktree ineligibility permits bypass;
            # busy slots cannot authorize extending that predecessor epoch.
            # Likewise, later small fixed jobs must not continuously refill the
            # slots an older wide claim needs. This reserves queue order only;
            # the waiter still acquires its complete real claim atomically.
            return True
        acquired = try_shared_slots(slots, needed)
        if not acquired:
            return False
        for _, fd, _ in acquired:
            os.close(fd)
        return True
    finally:
        if worktree_fd is not None:
            os.close(worktree_fd)


class AdmissionWaiter:
    """FIFO among registered, eligible waiters; an OS lease proves each is live.

    A ticket is registered before an ordinary command waits for memory.
    Registration holds no CPU or worktree resources. No PID liveness guess,
    watchdog or child process is needed: death closes its lease, and the next
    registry reader retires the stale ticket. The ticket is never inherited by
    the admitted command; only the existing pool/worktree leases survive it.
    """

    def __init__(self, label, worktree=None, slots=1, exclusive=False, memory=0, needed=1,
                 arrival_ns=None):
        self.label, self.path, self.fd = label, None, None
        self.arrival_ns = arrival_ns
        self.required = {"worktree": worktree, "slots": slots,
                         "exclusive": exclusive, "memory": memory, "needed": needed}

    def __enter__(self):
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *_):
        self.close()

    def register(self):
        # Share the exact live-lease scan and arrival order with acquisition;
        # registration alone cannot return or transfer a resource claim.
        self.attempt(None, None)

    def close(self):
        if self.fd is not None:
            with admission_registry():
                self.retire()

    def retire(self):
        """Retire while the caller holds the registry lock."""
        try:
            try:
                if not same_waiter_file(self.fd, self.path):
                    raise OSError("admission ticket changed during retirement")
                os.unlink(self.path)
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass
        finally:
            os.close(self.fd)
            self.fd = None

    def pending_reservation(self, live, available):
        """Hold temporary minimum probes only; never transfer a peer grant."""
        protected = []
        try:
            for _, path in sorted(live):
                if path == self.path:
                    continue
                try:
                    required = read_admission_requirements(path)
                    worktree = required["worktree"]
                    slots, needed = required["slots"], required.get("needed", 1)
                    exclusive = required["exclusive"]
                    if required["native"] and not isinstance(available, NativeMemoryObservation):
                        return self.required["slots"], protected
                except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OverflowError, RecursionError):
                    return self.required["slots"], protected
                # Our minimum and shared admission are already held. Exclusive
                # work cannot overlap; withholding extras cannot admit it.
                if exclusive or not waiter_eligible(path, available):
                    continue
                # Counts alone could leave only a high slot outside a peer's
                # smaller configured pool. Retain the actual eligible minimum
                # under registry custody until our optional borrowing finishes.
                claim = try_shared_slots(slots, needed)
                if claim:
                    protected.extend(claim)
            return 0, protected
        except BaseException:
            for _, fd, _ in protected:
                os.close(fd)
            raise

    def attempt(self, acquire, available, *, draining=False, borrow=False):
        # Keep eligibility probing and full resource acquisition atomic with
        # respect to other queue readers. No queued waiter holds a worktree.
        with admission_registry() as directory:
            live = []
            for name in os.listdir(directory):
                if not name.startswith("wait-") or not name[5:].isdigit():
                    continue
                path = os.path.join(directory, name)
                order = int(name[5:])
                if path == self.path:
                    live.append((order, path))
                    continue
                try:
                    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
                except FileNotFoundError:
                    continue
                try:
                    try:
                        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                    except BlockingIOError:
                        live.append((order, path))
                    else:
                        if not same_waiter_file(fd, path):
                            raise OSError("admission ticket changed while checking its lease")
                        os.unlink(path)
                finally:
                    os.close(fd)
            if self.fd is None:
                if self.arrival_ns is None:
                    order = next_admission_order(directory, [item[0] for item in live])
                else:
                    # A memory rollback must not turn an older command into
                    # a new arrival behind a sustained stream of small jobs.
                    order = self.arrival_ns
                    while os.path.exists(os.path.join(directory, f"wait-{order}")):
                        order += 1
                self.path = os.path.join(directory, f"wait-{order}")
                self.fd = os.open(self.path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
                fcntl.flock(self.fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
                os.write(self.fd, json.dumps({"pid": os.getpid(), "cmd": self.label,
                                             "cwd": os.getcwd(),
                                             "started": time.time(),
                                             "requires": self.required}).encode())
            if acquire is None:
                return None
            order = int(os.path.basename(self.path)[5:])
            if any(prior < order and waiter_eligible(path, available, draining=draining)
                   for prior, path in live):
                return None
            acquired = (acquire(lambda: self.pending_reservation(live, available))
                        if borrow else acquire())
            if acquired:
                self.retire()
            return acquired


class NativeEpochWaiter:
    """Reserve the existing canonical FIFO/barrier before draining legacy work.

    This is an epoch transition, not a user exclusive benchmark or a CPU grant.
    Existing native peers still share the same SH fence when no ticket is ahead.
    """

    def __init__(self, directory, slots, label, memory, worktree=None, arrival_ns=None):
        self.directory, self.slots, self.memory = directory, slots, memory
        self.worktree, self.worktree_fd, self.barrier = worktree, None, None
        self.ready_fence = None
        self.waiter = AdmissionWaiter("native epoch: " + label, worktree=worktree,
                                      slots=exclusive_slot_count(slots), exclusive=True, memory=memory,
                                      arrival_ns=arrival_ns)

    def __enter__(self):
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *_):
        self.close()

    def close(self):
        try:
            self.waiter.close()
        finally:
            self.release_claim()

    def release_claim(self):
        if self.ready_fence is not None:
            for fd in self.ready_fence:
                os.close(fd)
            self.ready_fence = None
        for name in ("barrier", "worktree_fd"):
            fd = getattr(self, name)
            if fd is not None:
                os.close(fd)
                setattr(self, name, None)

    def take_worktree(self):
        fd, self.worktree_fd = self.worktree_fd, None
        return fd

    def reserve(self):
        # Full claim under the registry: never wait with only a worktree lease.
        # Keeping it through the native claim also prevents a fixed waiter from
        # holding this worktree while waiting on our newly shared epoch fence.
        if self.worktree:
            self.worktree_fd = try_lease(self.worktree)
            if self.worktree_fd is None:
                return None
        try:
            # Called only after FIFO eligibility is adjudicated under the same
            # registry lock. Our own/younger tickets cannot forbid a compatible
            # native join; older memory/worktree-eligible fixed work still wins.
            self.ready_fence = try_legacy_fence(self.directory, self.slots, priority=True)
            if self.ready_fence is not None:
                return self.ready_fence
            root = checked_cpu_directory(self.directory)
            try:
                self.barrier = checked_legacy_fence_file(root, "admission.lock")
            finally:
                os.close(root)
            fcntl.flock(self.barrier, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            if active_adoption(os.path.join(self.directory, "admission.lock")) is not None:
                raise BlockingIOError()
            os.ftruncate(self.barrier, 0)
            os.write(self.barrier, json.dumps({"pid": os.getpid(), "cmd": self.waiter.label,
                                              "cwd": os.getcwd(), "started": time.time(),
                                              "native_epoch_transition": True}).encode())
            return [self.barrier]
        except BlockingIOError:
            self.release_claim()
            return None
        except BaseException:
            self.release_claim()
            raise

    def attempt(self, available):
        # This transition has not started a command. If its measured memory
        # eligibility disappears while old holders drain, release its barrier
        # and worktree claim so eligible work can proceed. Retrying rejoins FIFO.
        if available is not None and available < self.memory:
            self.release_claim()
            return None
        if self.barrier is None:
            # Preserve the ordinary memory precondition before reserving any
            # legacy leases. An ineligible transition must not idle fixed work.
            if self.waiter.path is None:
                can_join = True
                if self.worktree:
                    self.worktree_fd = try_lease(self.worktree)
                    can_join = self.worktree_fd is not None
                if can_join:
                    try:
                        fence = try_legacy_fence(self.directory, self.slots)
                        if fence is not None:
                            return fence
                    except BaseException:
                        self.release_claim()
                        raise
                    self.release_claim()
                # Busy worktrees still get tickets. They do not block other
                # eligible work, and recover their FIFO turn when they free.
            claim = self.waiter.attempt(self.reserve, available, draining=True)
            if not claim:
                return None
            if self.ready_fence is not None:
                fence, self.ready_fence = self.ready_fence, None
                return fence
        try:
            fence = try_legacy_fence(self.directory, self.slots, self.barrier)
        except EpochReservationLost:
            self.release_claim()
            return None
        if fence is not None:
            self.barrier = None  # ownership transfers to the native child fence
        return fence


def write_adoption(path, info):
    import tempfile

    pending = None
    try:
        with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode="w", dir=os.path.dirname(path),
                                         prefix=".build-slot-adopt-", delete=False) as stream:
            pending = stream.name
            json.dump(info, stream)
            stream.flush()
            os.fsync(stream.fileno())
        os.replace(pending, path)
    finally:
        if pending and os.path.exists(pending):
            os.unlink(pending)


def prior_adoption(identity, worktree):
    for _, info in adoption_records():
        if "identity" not in info:
            raise IdentityError("adoption registry is unreadable")
        if same_process(identity, info["identity"]):
            if info.get("worktree") != worktree or info.get("pool") != os.path.realpath(DIR):
                raise IdentityError("process is already adopted in another pool or worktree")
            return info
    return None


def checked_adoption_identity(pid):
    identity = process_identity(pid)
    if identity is None:
        raise IdentityError("process has exited")
    if identity["uid"] != os.geteuid():
        raise IdentityError("process is owned by another user")
    if os.path.realpath(process_cwd(pid)) != os.path.realpath(os.getcwd()):
        raise IdentityError("run adopt from the direct job's exact working directory")
    after = process_identity(pid)
    if after != identity:
        raise IdentityError("process changed during adoption identity checks")
    return identity


def adopt(pid, slots, mem_gib, per_worktree, exclusive):
    """One atomic full-claim record, no watcher and no inherited admission."""
    import hashlib

    worktree = worktree_lock_path() if per_worktree else None
    worktree = os.path.realpath(worktree) if worktree else None
    announced = False
    count = exclusive_slot_count(slots) if exclusive else slots
    waiter = AdmissionWaiter(f"adopt {pid}", worktree, count, exclusive, mem_gib)
    try:
        identity = checked_adoption_identity(pid)
        namespace_directory(ADOPTION_DIR)
        namespace_directory(DIR)
        while True:
            current = process_identity(pid)
            if current is None or not same_process(current, identity):
                raise IdentityError("process exited or its PID was reused while waiting")
            if current["uid"] != os.geteuid():
                raise IdentityError("process is no longer owned by this user")
            # Serialize only registration attempts. Ordinary admission reads
            # atomic records under its own lease flock; it needs no new lock.
            registration = os.open(os.path.join(ADOPTION_DIR, "registration.lock"),
                                   os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
            leases = []
            try:
                try:
                    fcntl.flock(registration, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                    prior = prior_adoption(identity, worktree)
                    if prior:
                        if exclusive and not prior.get("exclusive"):
                            raise IdentityError("existing shared adoption cannot be upgraded")
                        print(f"build-slot: already adopted pid={pid}")
                        return 0
                    avail = available_gib()
                    if avail is None or avail >= mem_gib:
                        claimed = waiter.attempt(
                            lambda: try_resources(worktree, count, exclusive), avail)
                        if not claimed:
                            raise BlockingIOError()
                        leases = claimed
                        fresh = checked_adoption_identity(pid)
                        if not same_process(fresh, identity):
                            raise IdentityError("process changed before adoption publication")
                        info = {"schema": 1, "adopted": True, "identity": fresh, "pid": pid,
                                "cmd": fresh["executable"], "cwd": os.getcwd(),
                                "started": time.time(), "exclusive": exclusive,
                                "pool": os.path.realpath(DIR), "worktree": worktree,
                                "leases": [os.path.realpath(path) for path, _ in leases]}
                        key = hashlib.sha256(f"{pid}:{identity['birth']}".encode()).hexdigest()
                        write_adoption(os.path.join(ADOPTION_DIR, key + ".json"), info)
                        print(f"build-slot: adopted pid={pid} leases={len(leases)}")
                        return 0
                except BlockingIOError:
                    pass
            finally:
                for _, fd in leases:
                    os.close(fd)
                os.close(registration)
            if not announced:
                print("build-slot: waiting for normal adoption admission", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
                announced = True
            time.sleep(2)
    except (IdentityError, OSError) as error:
        print(f"build-slot: adoption refused: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    finally:
        waiter.close()


def queued_status(directory=None):
    if directory is None:
        directory = DIR if DIR is not None else slot_directory()
    """Observe live ticket leases without creating, retiring or claiming one."""
    directory = os.path.join(os.path.realpath(directory), "admission")
    try:
        registry = os.open(os.path.join(directory, "registry.lock"),
                           os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return [], 0, None
    except OSError as error:
        return [], 0, str(error)
    rows, stale = [], 0
    try:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(registry).st_mode):
            return [], 0, "admission registry is not a regular file"
        try:
            fcntl.flock(registry, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            return [], 0, "admission registry is busy"
        for name in os.listdir(directory):
            if not name.startswith("wait-") or not name[5:].isascii() or not name[5:].isdigit():
                continue
            path = os.path.join(directory, name)
            record = {}
            try:
                fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
                try:
                    if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
                        raise OSError("admission ticket is not a regular file")
                    try:
                        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                    except BlockingIOError:
                        if not same_waiter_file(fd, path):
                            raise OSError("admission ticket changed during observation")
                        data = os.read(fd, 65537)
                        if len(data) > 65536:
                            raise ValueError("admission ticket exceeds observation bound")
                        record = decode_admission_record(data)
                    else:
                        stale += 1
                        continue
                finally:
                    os.close(fd)
            except FileNotFoundError:
                continue
            except (OSError, ValueError, RecursionError) as error:
                record = {"observation_error": str(error)}
            rows.append((int(name[5:]), record))
        return sorted(rows, key=lambda row: row[0]), stale, None
    except OSError as error:
        return rows, stale, str(error)
    finally:
        os.close(registry)


def print_exclusive_reservation(directory=None):
    if directory is None:
        directory = DIR if DIR is not None else slot_directory()
    """Observe an exclusive winner that left the queue to drain the slot pool."""
    path = os.path.join(os.path.realpath(directory), "admission.lock")
    try:
        fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NONBLOCK | getattr(os, "O_NOFOLLOW", 0))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return
    except OSError as error:
        print(f"reservation: observation unavailable ({error})")
        return
    try:
        if not stat.S_ISREG(os.fstat(fd).st_mode):
            raise OSError("admission lease is not a regular file")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except BlockingIOError:
            if not same_waiter_file(fd, path):
                raise OSError("admission lease changed during observation")
            data = os.read(fd, 65537)
            if len(data) > 65536:
                raise ValueError("admission lease exceeds observation bound")
            record = json.loads(data)
            if not isinstance(record, dict):
                raise ValueError("admission lease is not an object")
            print(f"reservation: exclusive=1 claim=all pid={record.get('pid')} "
                  f"cwd={json.dumps(record.get('cwd'))} cmd={json.dumps(record.get('cmd'))}; "
                  "shared launches wait while this lease is held")
    except (OSError, ValueError, RecursionError) as error:
        print(f"reservation: observation unavailable ({error})")
    finally:
        os.close(fd)


def print_queued_status(directory=None):
    rows, stale, error = queued_status(directory)
    if error:
        print(f"queue: observation unavailable ({error}); admission rules unchanged")
        return
    print(f"queue: {len(rows)} pending request(s), {stale} stale ticket(s) ignored; "
          "oldest eligible first; eligible exclusive requests reserve the whole pool")
    for position, (_, record) in enumerate(rows):
        try:
            required = admission_requirements(record)
            if record.get("observation_error"):
                raise ValueError("unreadable admission record")
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, OverflowError, RecursionError):
            print(f"wait {position}: requirements unavailable; "
                  "no eligibility or capacity claim can be made")
            continue
        exclusive = required.get("exclusive")
        exclusive_text = str(int(exclusive)) if isinstance(exclusive, bool) else "?"
        needed = required.get("needed", 1)
        pool_slots = required.get("slots")
        if exclusive is True:
            claim = "all"
        elif (exclusive is False and type(needed) is int and type(pool_slots) is int
              and 1 <= needed <= pool_slots):
            claim = "one" if needed == 1 else str(needed)
        else:
            claim = "unknown"
        print(f"wait {position}: pid={record.get('pid')} exclusive={exclusive_text} "
              f"claim={claim} pool_slots={required.get('slots')} "
              f"mem_gib={required.get('memory')} "
              f"cwd={json.dumps(record.get('cwd'))} "
              f"worktree_lock={json.dumps(required.get('worktree'))} "
              f"cmd={json.dumps(record.get('cmd'))}")


def status(slots, directory=None):
    if directory is None:
        directory = DIR if DIR is not None else slot_directory()
    if ADOPTION_DIR is None:
        print("build-slot: canonical user home is unavailable", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    namespace_directory(directory)
    avail = available_gib()
    print(f"slots={slots} cpus={NCPU} load1={load1():.1f} avail_gib={avail if avail is None else round(avail, 1)} dir={directory}")
    free_slots = 0
    for i in range(slots):
        p = os.path.join(directory, f"slot-{i}")
        held = False
        info = {}
        try:
            fd = os.open(p, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o644)
            try:
                fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                adopted = active_adoption(p)
                if adopted is not None:
                    held = True
                    info = adopted
                fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
            except BlockingIOError:
                held = True
                try:
                    fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_SH | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                except BlockingIOError:
                    pass
                else:
                    # An EX failure does not identify the old JSON writer:
                    # native epochs retain SH exclusion without rewriting it.
                    # Recheck EX after SH so a holder retiring between probes
                    # does not manufacture a shared fence from our own lock.
                    try:
                        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
                    except BlockingIOError:
                        info = {"shared_exclusion": True}
                    else:
                        held = False
                        adopted = active_adoption(p)
                        if adopted is not None:
                            held, info = True, adopted
                        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
            finally:
                os.close(fd)
        except OSError:
            held = True
            info = {"pid": None, "cmd": "lease status unavailable; held fail-closed"}
        info = info or (holder_info(p) if held else {})
        if held:
            if info.get("shared_exclusion"):
                print(f"slot {i}: HELD mode=shared-exclusion pid=None age=unknown "
                      "cwd=None cmd=shared-exclusion-fence cpu_budget=unknown; "
                      "previous slot record is not current owner attribution")
                continue
            age = int(time.time() - info.get("started", time.time()))
            adopted = " adopted=1" if info.get("adopted") else ""
            budget = info.get("cpu_budget")
            budget = budget if type(budget) is int and budget > 0 else "unknown"
            print(f"slot {i}: HELD pid={info.get('pid')} age={age}s cwd={info.get('cwd')} cmd={info.get('cmd')}{adopted} cpu_budget={budget}")
        else:
            free_slots += 1
            print(f"slot {i}: free")
    print(f"capacity: free_slots={free_slots} pool_slots={slots} "
          f"default_cpu_budget={max(1, NCPU // slots)} observed_cpu_use=unknown; "
          "snapshot only; memory, worktree and queue eligibility still apply")
    print_exclusive_reservation(directory)
    print_queued_status(directory)
    return 0


def usage():
    print("usage: build-slot [--exclusive] [--wait-timeout S] [--cpus N] [--slots N] [--mem-gb G] [--no-worktree-lock] [--rank ordinary|release] [--claim-key K] [--wide] -- <command> [args...]\n       build-slot [options] adopt PID\n       build-slot status\n       build-slot --capabilities", file=sys.stderr)


class ExecutionStart:
    """One original private pipe reports dispatch DATA, never CPU authority.

    The admitted payload never inherits this writer. The receiver can separate
    a finite queue wait from its execution budget without inspecting markers,
    stderr, ledger counts or another process's claimed readiness.
    """
    def __init__(self, raw):
        try:
            if (not raw.isascii() or not raw.isdigit()
                    or not 3 <= int(raw) <= 2147483647):
                raise ValueError
            self.fd = int(raw)
            held = os.fstat(self.fd)
            flags = fcntl.fcntl(self.fd, fcntl.F_GETFL)
            if (not stat.S_ISFIFO(held.st_mode)
                    or flags & os.O_ACCMODE != os.O_WRONLY
                    or not flags & os.O_NONBLOCK):
                raise ValueError
            self.identity = (held.st_dev, held.st_ino, held.st_mode)
            os.set_inheritable(self.fd, False)
        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
            raise NamespaceError("execution-start requires an original nonblocking writable pipe") from error

    def notify(self, pid, started_us):
        fd, self.fd = self.fd, None
        try:
            held = os.fstat(fd)
            if (held.st_dev, held.st_ino, held.st_mode) != self.identity:
                raise ValueError("execution-start pipe changed")
            message = b"S" + pid.to_bytes(8, "big") + started_us.to_bytes(8, "big")
            if os.write(fd, message) != len(message):
                raise ValueError("incomplete execution-start notification")
        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
            raise NamespaceError(f"execution-start notification refused: {error}") from error
        finally:
            os.close(fd)


def main(argv):
    # Close only descriptors transferred to this invocation. A child keeps its
    # inherited descriptions until actual exit; never explicitly unlock them.
    owned = set()
    try:
        return _main(argv, owned)
    finally:
        for fd in owned:
            os.close(fd)


def _main(argv, owned):
    global DIR
    slots = default_slots()
    mem_gib = float(os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_MEM_GB", "8"))
    # Only a caller's own figure is claimed as memory in aterm's ledger; the
    # default 8 GiB is the pool's admission floor, not a measurement.
    mem_explicit = "BUILD_SLOT_MEM_GB" in os.environ
    per_worktree = True
    exclusive = False
    wide = False
    wait_timeout = None
    execution_start = None
    cpus = None
    memory_attempt = None
    memory_arrival = None
    memory_since_ms = None
    rank = "ordinary"
    claim_key = None
    if argv == ["--capabilities"]:
        # Answered before any namespace, admission or environment is read: an
        # older copy refuses this as an unknown option and starts nothing.
        print(CLAIM_WORDS_PROTOCOL)
        return 0
    if argv[:1] == ["--_ledger-quiet"]:
        # Exec'd by `aterm pkg claim` under an exclusive (ALONE) claim.
        return ledger_quiet_exec(argv[1:])
    if argv[:1] == ["status"]:
        DIR = slot_directory()
        runtime = os.path.join(DIR, "runtime-v2")
        if os.path.isdir(runtime):
            print("legacy pool (native epochs hold shared exclusion fences here):")
            result = status(slots)
            print("native runtime-v2 pool:")
            result = max(result, status(slots, runtime))
        else:
            result = status(slots)
        if result == 0:  # a refused status reports nothing on stdout
            print_admission_authority()
        return result
    args = list(argv)
    cmd = None
    options = []
    adopt_pid = None
    while args:
        a = args.pop(0)
        if a == "--":
            cmd = args
            options = list(argv[:len(argv) - len(args) - 1])
            break
        if a == "--slots":
            slots = int(args.pop(0))
        elif a == "--cpus":
            if (not args or len(args[0]) > 4300 or not args[0].isascii()
                    or not args[0].isdigit() or not 1 <= int(args[0]) <= NCPU):
                print(f"build-slot: --cpus requires an integer from 1 to {NCPU}", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            cpus = int(args.pop(0))
        elif a == "--mem-gb":
            mem_gib = float(args.pop(0))
            mem_explicit = True
        elif a == "--wide":
            wide = True
        elif a == "--_memory-since-ms":
            # The coordinator's wall-clock arrival, for the ledger's one look.
            if (not args or not args[0].isascii() or not args[0].isdigit()
                    or len(args[0]) > 20 or int(args[0]) < 1):
                print("build-slot: coordinated admission needs a positive arrival time", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            memory_since_ms = int(args.pop(0))
        elif a == "--_memory-attempt":
            try:
                memory_attempt = int(args.pop(0))
                memory_arrival = int(args.pop(0))
                held = os.environ.get("HEAVY_GATE_HELD", "").partition(":")
                if (memory_attempt < 3 or not 0 < memory_arrival < 10**39
                        or not held[0].isdigit()
                        or int(held[0]) < 1 or not held[2]
                        or not stat.S_ISFIFO(os.fstat(memory_attempt).st_mode)):
                    raise ValueError
            except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
                print("build-slot: coordinated admission needs a held memory reservation and reply pipe", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
        elif a == "--no-worktree-lock":
            per_worktree = False
        elif a == "--rank":
            if not args or args[0] not in RANKS:
                print("build-slot: --rank takes ordinary or release; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            rank = args.pop(0)
        elif a == "--claim-key":
            if not args or not CLAIM_KEY.fullmatch(args[0]):
                print("build-slot: --claim-key takes 1 to 200 of [A-Za-z0-9._:/@+-], starting with a "
                      "letter or digit; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            claim_key = args.pop(0)
        elif a == "--exclusive":
            exclusive = True
        elif a == "--execution-start-fd":
            if execution_start is not None or not args:
                raise NamespaceError("execution-start requires one original pipe")
            execution_start = ExecutionStart(args.pop(0))
        elif a == "--wait-timeout":
            try:
                wait_timeout = float(args.pop(0))
                if not math.isfinite(wait_timeout) or wait_timeout <= 0:
                    raise ValueError
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                print("build-slot: --wait-timeout needs positive finite seconds; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
        elif a == "adopt":
            if len(args) != 1 or not args[0].isdigit() or int(args[0]) < 1 or slots < 1:
                print("build-slot: adopt requires one positive PID and a positive slot count", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            adopt_pid = int(args[0])
            cmd = ["adopt", args[0]]
            break
        elif a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__)
            return 0
        elif a.startswith("-"):
            print(f"build-slot: unknown option {a!r}; no command was started. "
                  "Use -- before a command beginning with '-'.", file=sys.stderr)
            usage()
            return 2
        else:
            cmd = [a] + args
            options = list(argv[:len(argv) - len(args) - 1])
            break
    if not cmd:
        usage()
        return 2
    if wide and (cpus is not None or exclusive or adopt_pid is not None):
        print("build-slot: --wide asks for the host's cores itself; it takes no --cpus, --exclusive "
              "or adopt; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if memory_since_ms is not None and memory_attempt is None:
        print("build-slot: an arrival time belongs to a coordinated attempt; no command was started",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    # Reject malformed hidden fronts before fixed/exclusive admission can run
    # them. Ordinary non-Targo commands retain their existing admission path.
    worker_invocation(cmd)
    original_resources = inherited_resource_fds(os.environ)
    if execution_start is not None:
        for fd in original_resources:
            original = os.fstat(fd)
            if (original.st_dev, original.st_ino, original.st_mode) == execution_start.identity:
                raise NamespaceError("execution-start pipe aliases original scheduling transport")
    if "BUILD_SLOT_FENCE_FDS" in os.environ and not (
            os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_HELD") == "1"
            and os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_PROTOCOL") == "2"):
        raise NamespaceError("inherited fences require their existing native epoch; "
                             "fresh admission cannot replace or mix them")
    if wait_timeout is not None and adopt_pid is not None:
        print("build-slot: --wait-timeout cannot bound an already running adopted job; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if exclusive and slots < 1:
        print("build-slot: --exclusive requires a positive slot count", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if cpus is not None and adopt_pid is not None:
        print("build-slot: --cpus cannot change an already running adopted job", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    wrapper = memory_wrapper(cmd)
    if execution_start is not None and (adopt_pid is not None
            or (wrapper is not None and not exclusive)):
        raise NamespaceError("execution-start does not observe adoption or coordinated memory wrappers")
    if wait_timeout is not None and wrapper is not None and not exclusive:
        print("build-slot: --wait-timeout requires a new --exclusive command for a shared memory wrapper; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if memory_attempt is not None:
        if (adopt_pid is not None or exclusive or wait_timeout is not None
                or wrapper is not None or os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_HELD") == "1"):
            print("build-slot: coordinated CPU attempt requires a fresh command", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        os.write(memory_attempt, b"W")
    elif wrapper is not None and not exclusive and adopt_pid is None:
        if os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_HELD") == "1":
            print("build-slot: acquire memory before the outer CPU reservation", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    if os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_HELD") == "1":
        if adopt_pid is not None:
            print("build-slot: adopt must run outside an existing admission", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        native_epoch = os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_PROTOCOL") == "2"
        if native_epoch and (exclusive or not worker_capability(cmd)):
            print("build-slot: nested native epochs require an invocation accepted by the selected Targo; fixed or exclusive work must run outside the epoch", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if exclusive and os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_EXCLUSIVE") != "1":
            print("build-slot: nested --exclusive cannot upgrade shared admission; request it on the outermost invocation", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if wait_timeout is not None:
            print("build-slot: --wait-timeout requires a fresh admission outside the held slot; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        if cpus is not None:
            try:
                parent_jobs = cpu_jobs(1, os.environ.get("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS", "0"), budget=NCPU, strict=True)
                if cpus > parent_jobs and os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_SOURCE") == "ledger-grant":
                    # A pool parent held at least one share, so its callers' --cpus
                    # fit; a ledger grant can be one core. Narrow to the grant: the
                    # parent's claim is what bounds the machine, never this word.
                    print(f"build-slot: --cpus {cpus} narrowed to the parent's ledger grant of "
                          f"{parent_jobs}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
                    cpus = parent_jobs
                if cpus > parent_jobs:
                    raise ValueError("a nested command cannot enlarge its parent's CPU budget")
                os.environ["CARGO_BUILD_JOBS"] = str(cpus)
                os.environ["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_SOURCE"] = "caller-or-fixed-share"
                os.environ["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_BUDGET"] = str(cpus)
                _, cap = job_provenance(os.environ, cpus)
                os.environ["TARGO_CALLER_JOBS"] = str(cap)
                os.environ["TARGO_PLANNED_JOBS"] = str(cpus)
            except ValueError as exc:
                print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — {exc}; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
        if native_epoch:
            cmd = worker_command(cmd)
        if execution_start is not None:
            execution_start.notify(os.getpid(), time.clock_gettime_ns(time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC) // 1000)
        os.execvp(cmd[0], cmd)
    DIR = slot_directory()
    if os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_CPU_PROTOCOL") == "2":
        if (os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_V2_DIR") != os.path.join(DIR, "runtime-v2")
                or os.environ.get("BUILD_SLOT_LEGACY_DIR", DIR) != DIR):
            raise NamespaceError("inherited native CPU namespace is inconsistent")
    if ADOPTION_DIR is None:
        print("build-slot: canonical user home is unavailable", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        if (exclusive or cpus is not None) and (type(MEASURED_NCPU) is not int or MEASURED_NCPU < 1):
            raise ValueError("exclusive or explicit CPU admission requires a measured positive CPU count")
        if exclusive and (not math.isfinite(mem_gib) or mem_gib < 0):
            raise ValueError("--mem-gb must be finite and nonnegative")
        generated_jobs, caller_jobs = job_provenance(os.environ, cpus) if adopt_pid is None else (False, None)
        budget = cpus if cpus is not None else (NCPU if exclusive else None)
        jobs = cpu_jobs(slots, os.environ.get("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS"), budget=budget,
                        strict=cpus is not None and not generated_jobs) if adopt_pid is None else None
        if jobs is not None and caller_jobs is not None:
            jobs = min(jobs, caller_jobs)
        # A ledger claim asks for the explicit --cpus, the host's cores for
        # --exclusive or --wide, else one pool share, under the same caller
        # caps. The ledger grants up to what is free and the grant is held for
        # the whole run, so an uncapped test, push or script must not ask for
        # the machine. The ledger's grant may be smaller than what is asked.
        ledger_budget = (cpus if cpus is not None else NCPU if exclusive or wide
                         else max(1, NCPU // (slots if slots > 0 else default_slots())))
        ledger_cores = cpu_jobs(1, os.environ.get("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS"), budget=ledger_budget,
                                strict=cpus is not None and not generated_jobs) if adopt_pid is None else None
        if ledger_cores is not None and caller_jobs is not None:
            ledger_cores = min(ledger_cores, caller_jobs)
    except ValueError as exc:
        print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — {exc}; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if wrapper is not None and not exclusive and memory_attempt is None and adopt_pid is None:
        return coordinate_memory(options, wrapper)
    # One admission authority: where aterm's capacity ledger can hold this
    # command's one covering claim, it alone admits, and no slot is taken.
    try:
        ledger = admission_ledger()
    except LedgerRefused as unknown:
        print(f"build-slot: REFUSED — which authority admits here is unknown ({unknown}); "
              "no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    if adopt_pid is not None:
        if ledger is not None:
            # An adopted slot is a pool record the ledger would have to count
            # for this job to be seen; start the job under build-slot instead.
            print("build-slot: REFUSED — adopt records a slot in the build-slot pool, and this host "
                  "admits through aterm's capacity ledger; run the job under build-slot instead",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        return adopt(adopt_pid, slots, mem_gib, per_worktree, exclusive)
    if ledger is not None:
        return ledger_admit_and_run(
            ledger, cmd, owned, legacy_dir=DIR, cores=ledger_cores, mem_gib=mem_gib,
            mem_explicit=mem_explicit, exclusive=exclusive, per_worktree=per_worktree,
            wait_timeout=wait_timeout, memory_attempt=memory_attempt,
            memory_since_ms=memory_since_ms, execution_start=execution_start,
            rank=rank, claim_key=claim_key)

    automatic = (cpus is None and not exclusive
                 and ("CARGO_BUILD_JOBS" not in os.environ or generated_jobs)
                 and type(MEASURED_NCPU) is int and MEASURED_NCPU > 0)
    workers = (not exclusive and type(MEASURED_NCPU) is int and MEASURED_NCPU > 0
               and worker_capability(cmd))
    own_args = cmd[1:cmd.index("--", 1)] if "--" in cmd[1:] else cmd[1:]
    if os.path.basename(cmd[0]) == "targo" and "--resource-worker-v2" in own_args and not workers:
        print("build-slot: selected compiler cohort does not support the requested native worker protocol; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    cpu_mode = "workers-v1" if workers else "fixed-v1"
    lease_id = secrets.token_hex(16)
    cpu_pool = exclusive_slot_count(slots) if cpus is not None else slots
    share = max(1, NCPU // cpu_pool)
    needed = min(cpu_pool, (cpus + share - 1) // share) if cpus is not None else 1
    namespace_directory(DIR)
    held_fds = []
    fence_fds = []
    legacy_dir = DIR
    label = " ".join(cmd)[:300]
    announced = set()
    deadline = time.monotonic() + wait_timeout if wait_timeout is not None else None

    def say(key, msg):
        if key not in announced:
            announced.add(key)
            print(f"build-slot: {msg}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)

    def check_deadline():
        if deadline is not None and time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            raise AdmissionTimeout

    def wait(seconds):
        if memory_attempt is not None:
            raise AdmissionUnavailable
        check_deadline()
        if deadline is not None:
            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                raise AdmissionTimeout
            seconds = min(seconds, remaining)
        time.sleep(seconds)

    def stamp(fd):
        os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
        os.write(fd, json.dumps({"pid": os.getpid(), "cmd": label, "cwd": os.getcwd(), "started": time.time()}).encode())

    worktree = worktree_lock_path() if per_worktree else None
    epoch_worktree_fd = None
    if workers:
        # An invalid original CPU manifest cannot be repaired by an epoch wait.
        # This is only a nonblocking preflight; admission and workers still
        # revalidate their actual descriptors before granting or executing.
        try:
            native_cpu_room(legacy_dir, NCPU, exclusive_slot_count(slots))
        except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
            raise CpuBridgeUnavailable(f"native CPU accounting unavailable: {error}") from error
        with NativeEpochWaiter(legacy_dir, slots, label, mem_gib, worktree,
                               arrival_ns=memory_arrival) as epoch:
            while True:
                check_deadline()
                fence_fds = epoch.attempt(available_gib())
                if fence_fds is not None:
                    owned.update(fence_fds)
                    epoch_worktree_fd = epoch.take_worktree()
                    if epoch_worktree_fd is not None:
                        owned.add(epoch_worktree_fd)
                        held_fds.append(epoch_worktree_fd)
                    break
                say("legacy-fence", "waiting: native epoch needs an eligible FIFO turn and legacy CPU drain")
                wait(0.05)
        DIR = os.path.join(legacy_dir, "runtime-v2")
        namespace_directory(DIR)
        checked = checked_cpu_directory(DIR, private=True)
        os.close(checked)

    # Retain the canonical gate's memory precondition before reserving leases.
    # Unknown measurements also wait fail-closed for an exclusive command.
    if exclusive:
        while True:
            check_deadline()
            avail = available_gib()
            if avail is not None and math.isfinite(avail) and avail >= mem_gib:
                break
            say("initial-mem", f"waiting: memory {avail} GiB available < {mem_gib:g} GiB needed or unavailable")
            wait(2)

    # Fixed commands register before taking a worktree lease; native commands
    # reuse the lease already secured with their epoch. Acquire the full weighted
    # claim at once. An eligible exclusive winner reserves the
    # existing admission barrier, then drains the canonical/historic slot pool.
    claim_worktree = None if epoch_worktree_fd is not None else worktree
    count = exclusive_slot_count(slots) if exclusive else cpu_pool
    admission_path = os.path.join(DIR, "admission.lock")
    with AdmissionWaiter(label, claim_worktree, count, exclusive, mem_gib, needed,
                         arrival_ns=memory_arrival if not workers else None) as waiter:
        waiter.register()
        while True:
            check_deadline()
            avail = available_gib()
            if (exclusive and (avail is None or not math.isfinite(avail))
                    or avail is not None and avail < mem_gib):
                say("mem", f"waiting: {avail} GiB available < {mem_gib:g} GiB needed or unavailable")
                wait(2 if exclusive else 10)
                continue
            try:
                # An uncapped caller borrows currently idle slots atomically.
                # Each additional share requires the same measured memory
                # headroom as the first. Unknown memory retains one share.
                maximum = 1
                if automatic and not workers and avail is not None and math.isfinite(avail) and mem_gib > 0:
                    maximum = max(1, min(count, int(avail // mem_gib)))
                acquired = waiter.attempt(
                    lambda pending=None: try_command_claim(
                        claim_worktree, count, exclusive, needed,
                        maximum if automatic else None, pending),
                    avail, borrow=automatic and not workers)
            except BlockingIOError as error:
                if error.args == ("worktree",):
                    info = holder_info(worktree)
                    say("wt", f"waiting: another build-slot job runs in this worktree (pid={info.get('pid')} cmd={info.get('cmd')})")
                elif error.args == ("admission",):
                    say("admission", "waiting: an exclusive reservation owns admission")
                elif cpus is not None:
                    say("slot", f"waiting for {needed} of {count} slots for {cpus} CPUs")
                else:
                    say("slot", f"waiting for one of {count} slots")
                acquired = None
            else:
                if not acquired:
                    say("queue", "waiting: older eligible admission waiter first")
            if acquired:
                owned.update(fd for _, fd in acquired)
                for _, fd in acquired:
                    stamp(fd)
                    held_fds.append(fd)
                admission_fd = next(fd for path, fd in acquired if path == admission_path)
                break
            wait(2)

    if exclusive:
        while True:
            check_deadline()
            acquired = try_exclusive_slots(slots)
            if acquired is not None:
                owned.update(fd for _, fd, _ in acquired)
                for _, fd, _ in acquired:
                    stamp(fd)
                    held_fds.append(fd)
                break
            say("exclusive", f"waiting for all {len(pool_slots(slots))} canonical slots; draining legacy or adopted slot holders for exclusive reservation")
            wait(2)
        print(f"build-slot: reserved {len(acquired)} slots exclusively; waiting for host readiness", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        wait_until_quiet(mem_gib, check_deadline, wait, say)

    if not exclusive:
        held_fds.remove(admission_fd)
        owned.remove(admission_fd)
        os.close(admission_fd)

    env = dict(os.environ)
    env["BUILD_SLOT_HELD"] = "1"
    env["BUILD_SLOT_DIR"] = legacy_dir
    env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_EXCLUSIVE", None)
    if exclusive:
        env["BUILD_SLOT_EXCLUSIVE"] = "1"
    if automatic:
        reserved = sum(os.path.basename(path).startswith("slot-") for path, _ in acquired)
        # Native records retain epoch/launch custody, not fixed CPU shares.
        # Leave room for its scheduler to grow as actual global worker leases
        # become available; every dispatch still needs those real credits.
        # Fixed commands retain the exact backed-share ceiling instead.
        jobs = NCPU if workers else max(1, NCPU * reserved // count)
        if generated_jobs:
            jobs = min(jobs, int(os.environ["CARGO_BUILD_JOBS"]))
        if caller_jobs is not None:
            jobs = min(jobs, caller_jobs)
    env["CARGO_BUILD_JOBS"] = str(jobs)
    # This records provenance; it does not authorize descendants to exceed
    # their inherited reservation. Explicit caps remain caps at every layer.
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_SOURCE"] = "available-slots" if automatic else "caller-or-fixed-share"
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_BUDGET"] = str(jobs)
    env["TARGO_PLANNED_JOBS"] = str(jobs)
    if caller_jobs is None:
        env.pop("TARGO_CALLER_JOBS", None)
    else:
        env["TARGO_CALLER_JOBS"] = str(caller_jobs)
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_MODE"] = cpu_mode
    env["BUILD_SLOT_POOL_SLOTS"] = str(exclusive_slot_count(slots) if workers else count)
    env["BUILD_SLOT_CPU_PROTOCOL"] = "2" if workers else "1"
    if workers:
        env["BUILD_SLOT_LEGACY_DIR"] = legacy_dir
        env["BUILD_SLOT_V2_DIR"] = DIR
        env["BUILD_SLOT_V2_SLOTS"] = str(count)
        env["BUILD_SLOT_FENCE_FDS"] = ",".join(map(str, fence_fds))
    else:
        env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_LEGACY_DIR", None)
        env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_V2_DIR", None)
        env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_V2_SLOTS", None)
        env.pop("BUILD_SLOT_FENCE_FDS", None)
    info = {"pid": os.getpid(), "cmd": label, "cwd": os.getcwd(),
            "started": time.time(), "cpu_mode": cpu_mode, "cpu_budget": jobs,
            "pool_slots": count, "lease_id": lease_id}
    # Publish the fixed reservation BEFORE judging native room. New native
    # workers recheck these kernel-held records under the same manifest lock.
    for fd in held_fds:
        os.lseek(fd, 0, os.SEEK_SET)
        os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
        os.write(fd, json.dumps(info).encode())
    if not workers:
        while True:
            check_deadline()
            try:
                if native_cpu_room(DIR, NCPU, count):
                    break
                reason = "native workers are draining for the fixed CPU reservation"
            except (OSError, ValueError) as error:
                # Contention returns False above. Missing/malformed/replaced
                # accounting cannot become valid by retaining our claim and
                # spinning; refuse without granting or repairing capacity.
                raise CpuBridgeUnavailable(f"native CPU accounting unavailable: {error}") from error
            say("native-cpu", f"waiting: {reason}")
            wait(0.05)
    check_deadline()
    worker_cmd = worker_command(cmd) if workers else cmd
    launch = resource_command(worker_cmd, env)
    check_deadline()
    observe_exit = original_child_exit_observer()
    if observe_exit is None:
        return 2
    if memory_attempt is not None:
        os.write(memory_attempt, b"R")
        os.close(memory_attempt)
    execution_started_us = time.clock_gettime_ns(time.CLOCK_MONOTONIC) // 1000 if execution_start else None
    child = subprocess.Popen(
        launch, env=env, start_new_session=True,
        pass_fds=sorted({*held_fds, *fence_fds, *inherited_resource_fds(env)}))
    info.update(pid=child.pid, supervisor_pid=os.getpid())
    if exclusive:
        info["exclusive"] = True
    if cpus is not None:
        info["cpus"] = cpus
    for fd in held_fds:
        os.lseek(fd, 0, os.SEEK_SET)
        os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
        os.write(fd, json.dumps(info).encode())

    forwardable = child

    def forward(sig, _frame):
        if forwardable is not None:
            resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(forwardable.pid, sig)

    previous = {sig: signal.signal(sig, forward)
                for sig in (signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP)}
    notification_failed = False
    try:
        if execution_start is not None:
            try:
                execution_start.notify(child.pid, execution_started_us)
            except Exception as error:
                # The original child/group still belongs to us. A closed
                # receiver must not strand it or retire its claims early.
                notification_failed = True
                print(f"build-slot: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
                resource_transport_owner().signal_owned_group(child.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        observe_exit(child.pid)
        forwardable = None
        rc = child.wait()
    finally:
        forwardable = None
        for sig, handler in previous.items():
            signal.signal(sig, handler)
    return 2 if notification_failed else (128 - rc if rc < 0 else rc)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except NamespaceError as error:
        print(f"build-slot: namespace refused: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    except CpuBridgeUnavailable as error:
        print(f"build-slot: CPU admission refused: {error}", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    except AdmissionTimeout:
        print("build-slot: REFUSED — admission wait timed out; no command was started", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    except AdmissionUnavailable:
        sys.exit(75)
